WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.462
This program contains graphic language and imagery may not be suitable for all audiences. Viewer discretion is advised.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:18.893
[man 1] &lt;i&gt;After leaving China and traveling all over,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.895
&lt;i&gt;I found I wasn’t as stressed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:25.066
&lt;i&gt;I had never cast a vote in all my life.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:27.861
&lt;i&gt;This time I voted with my feet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:36.453
[reporter 1] &lt;i&gt;In the surge of migrants illegally crossing&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the Mexico-US border,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:40.290
&lt;i&gt;there’s now a growing number of&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Chinese nationals.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:44.544
[reporter 2] &lt;i&gt;Border patrol agents arrested&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;more than 24,000 Chinese people&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:49.049
&lt;i&gt;for crossing the US Southern border illegally&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;over the past year through September.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.633
[reporter 3] &lt;i&gt;Since October of last year (2022),&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.260
&lt;i&gt;the number of illegal immigrants&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;from China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.804
&lt;i&gt;now called "line walkers" by netizens,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:57.223
&lt;i&gt;has increased by 15 times compared with&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the same period last year,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.225
&lt;i&gt;reaching a historical peak.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:03.605
[reporter 4] &lt;i&gt;Why are Chinese people continuing to&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;“flee” to the United States,&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.023
&lt;i&gt;in spite of all the dangers and difficulties?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.152
[man 2] &lt;i&gt;Why did I wake up?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:11.654
&lt;i&gt;I feel like waking up was an agonizing process.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:13.198
The Chinese people want human rights!

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.533
The Chinese people want human rights!

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.994
[man 3]I'm already at the bottom of society, 
what do I fear?

00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:19.579
[man 4] In China, gays and lesbians cannot
get married or have children.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.373
When we grow old,
we will be left all alone.

00:01:22.373 --> 00:01:24.125
I’m afraid of being arrested when I talk,

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:25.168
when I do anything.

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:26.795
Democracy! Rule of law!

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:28.338
Freedom of speech!

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:31.257
We must persist in the Zero-Covid Policy
without wavering.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.511
[Xi] Launch a people's war, a total war,

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.221
-[Xi] against the epidemic.
-[Crowd] Lift the lockdown!

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.932
[man 5] The zero-COVID policy created Chinese refugees.

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.519
I just want my children

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.270
to live differently.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.731
&lt;i&gt;We want freedom!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.399
&lt;i&gt;We want freedom!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:07.669
After enduring China’s Covid-19 restrictions, many fled the country, taking perilous journeys through South and Central America to reach the United States. This route is referred to by Chinese internet users as “zouxian”, or “walk the line”.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:12.257
[Airport train announcing stops]

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.266
&lt;i&gt;At the end of 2022,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.059
&lt;i&gt;I first reported on Chinese citizens&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:25.103
&lt;i&gt;"walking the line" in Colombia.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:26.688
&lt;i&gt;Initially, I was going to interview&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:28.940
&lt;i&gt;Latin Americans who crossed&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the Darién Gap,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.943
&lt;i&gt;but unexpectedly I saw dozens of&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Chinese faces&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:33.653
&lt;i&gt;like mine at the port.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.036
&lt;i&gt;In March 2023,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:44.122
&lt;i&gt;I decided to follow in their footsteps.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.969
&lt;i&gt;I flew from my homeland, Taiwan,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:00.638
&lt;i&gt;to Istanbul, Turkey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:03.224
&lt;i&gt;Most Chinese who plan&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to walk the line&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:06.102
&lt;i&gt;will fly here from various ports in China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:09.147
&lt;i&gt;and then fly from Istanbul to Ecuador.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:11.858
&lt;i&gt;Ecuador is one of the few&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Latin American countries&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.861
&lt;i&gt;that Chinese passport holders can enter&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;without a visa.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:19.532
&lt;i&gt;As soon as I arrived at the boarding gate&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for my flight to Ecuador,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.410
&lt;i&gt;I saw about thirty Chinese,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.163
&lt;i&gt;including at least two families.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:27.665
&lt;i&gt;Are they all planning to&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;go to the United States?&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:32.253
I need to fight for my own future.

00:03:32.253 --> 00:03:35.006
The US is also divided into classes, right?

00:03:35.006 --> 00:03:37.508
You start in the lowest class,
no way around it.

00:03:37.508 --> 00:03:40.094
To get to the elite class,
you must fight for it with all you have.

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:42.555
So, when I get there,
I’ll have to struggle all over again,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.516
just like when I first graduated.

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:47.393
Of course, for me,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.230
I am already in my thirties,

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.482
and starting over

00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:54.150
was not an easy decision.

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:56.694
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;For these migrants,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:56.694 --> 00:03:59.906
&lt;i&gt;leaving China is a challenge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.784
&lt;i&gt;They are terrified of being interrogated&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;by Chinese customs&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:02.784 --> 00:04:05.036
&lt;i&gt;or even prevented from leaving.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:07.455
&lt;i&gt;First they would buy round-trip tickets&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:07.455 --> 00:04:09.332
&lt;i&gt;from China to Istanbul,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:12.794
&lt;i&gt;book hotels and travel itineraries&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in Turkey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:14.128
Once out of China&lt;i&gt;,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:14.128 --> 00:04:15.255
&lt;i&gt;they cancel their reservations&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.049
&lt;i&gt;and buy a ticket to Quito,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the capital of Ecuador.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:21.302
China is also divided into big cities
and small cities,

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:24.055
sensitive areas and not so sensitive areas.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:27.225
If you're from a sensitive area,
going to some sensitive places,

00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:28.935
Turkey is also a sensitive place now,

00:04:30.019 --> 00:04:32.855
if they fly there from China,

00:04:32.855 --> 00:04:35.233
they are likely to get stopped.

00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:37.694
I can't go into detail now,

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:41.364
because there are many
fellow Chinese here.

00:04:42.031 --> 00:04:43.700
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;After arriving in Ecuador,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.536
&lt;i&gt;migrants have to cross seven countries&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:46.536 --> 00:04:48.830
&lt;i&gt;and travel 3,500 kilometers north&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.290
&lt;i&gt;before reaching the United States.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.211
[Flight attendant announcing flight arrival]

00:04:58.381 --> 00:05:00.258
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;After 14 hours,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:02.176
&lt;i&gt;we completed the long international flight.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.637
&lt;i&gt;In the terminal,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.181
&lt;i&gt;we saw an old man in a neat suit&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:09.600
&lt;i&gt;and a young couple dressed in vacation attire.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:10.351 --> 00:05:13.813
&lt;i&gt;I found out that the reason&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;why they dressed up like this&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.815
&lt;i&gt;was because they were afraid that&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Ecuadorian customs would suspect them&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.276
&lt;i&gt;of being "fake tourists” there to walk the line,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:18.276 --> 00:05:19.944
&lt;i&gt;and they would be deported back to Turkey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:24.574 --> 00:05:26.200
[Mr. Li] I took a walk today 

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.869
Quito is quite mountainous.

00:05:27.869 --> 00:05:29.454
[Alicia] You had some altitude sickness?

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:30.371
Yeah, altitude sickness.

00:05:30.371 --> 00:05:31.539
I just had a headache,

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:34.542
and it felt like my brain was waterlogged,

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:37.420
like it was all clogged up.

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:43.134
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Walking into the colorful&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;bungalow community in central Quito,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:46.054
&lt;i&gt;there is a hostel hidden in an alley.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:48.473
&lt;i&gt;The hostel owner, also from China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:50.350
&lt;i&gt;provides travelers with a place to stay.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.269
&lt;i&gt;Twenty-five dollars a night,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;including meals.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:53.269 --> 00:05:54.896
&lt;i&gt;The hostel also sells&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;rainforest equipment,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:54.896 --> 00:05:57.607
&lt;i&gt;Chinese cigarettes,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and instant noodles.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:58.941
&lt;i&gt;In busy periods,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:58.941 --> 00:06:00.902
&lt;i&gt;it can host more than&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;30 people a night.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:05.531
&lt;i&gt;Most travelers will team up here&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.408
&lt;i&gt;and continue heading north together.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:10.453
Why should I team up with
other migrants

00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:12.830
and share my personal business

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.374
and share my personal business？

00:06:14.957 --> 00:06:16.793
I’m not seeking anything from them,

00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:20.213
I just hope they don’t bother me.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.134
These photos were taken some years ago.

00:06:25.134 --> 00:06:28.763
I’ve worked in hospitality for a few years.

00:06:28.763 --> 00:06:32.058
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; Mr. Li once worked as a hotel manager&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt; in Guangzhou.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.309
&lt;i&gt;Before setting off,&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:37.021
&lt;i&gt;he spent half a year researching&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;travel strategies on social media.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:39.649 --> 00:06:41.526
I saw these short videos

00:06:41.526 --> 00:06:44.987
about walking the line on Douyin

00:06:44.987 --> 00:06:47.281
in September last year.

00:06:48.366 --> 00:06:49.742
An opportunity to go to America.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:55.832
Yes. So I started planning at that time.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:01.254
If you decide to walk the line,

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.171
how much money do you need?

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:04.006
[Douyin] You can hide $500 in one shoe,

00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:05.216
$1,000 in a pair.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.385
Hold on to the rope!

00:07:08.886 --> 00:07:10.805
To be honest, I was still very reluctant

00:07:10.805 --> 00:07:11.681
until the very moment I left.

00:07:12.849 --> 00:07:14.559
The social environments are intolerable

00:07:14.642 --> 00:07:19.313
for any reasonable person.

00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:21.065
Unless I had family and loves ones

00:07:21.065 --> 00:07:21.983
keeping me in China,

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:23.317
I’d find a way to immigrate.

00:07:23.317 --> 00:07:24.610
Even if I did,

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.112
I’d figure out how to take them with me.

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:29.323
[Woman singing in Spanish]

00:07:40.001 --> 00:07:41.836
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In Quito Old Town,&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:41.836 --> 00:07:43.754
&lt;i&gt;I met a family of four preparing&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:43.754 --> 00:07:44.797
&lt;i&gt;to go to the Darién Gap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:45.423 --> 00:07:46.674
&lt;i&gt;The father was worried&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:46.674 --> 00:07:48.926
&lt;i&gt;about the safety of his family in China&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:48.926 --> 00:07:50.470
&lt;i&gt;and chose not to show his face .&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:51.012 --> 00:07:53.389
&lt;i&gt;He even worried that the Chinese government&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:56.100
&lt;i&gt;could identify him from the way he walks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:58.936 --> 00:08:00.271
Three years of Zero-Covid Policy.

00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:06.027
Many things were completely exposed.

00:08:06.027 --> 00:08:06.903
You lie...

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:08.654
No matter how good at lying you are,

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:11.616
do you really think we are that gullible?

00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:18.372
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;His nine-year-old daughter&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;was drinking a milkshake aside.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:18.372 --> 00:08:21.042
&lt;i&gt;and he teared up as he talked.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:24.545
&lt;i&gt;He used a VPN to bypass the Great Firewall&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;see the world without censorship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:24.545 --> 00:08:26.797
&lt;i&gt;He owned a bookstore&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:26.797 --> 00:08:28.758
&lt;i&gt;and was interrogated&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;by the National Security police.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:32.762 --> 00:08:36.682
They warned us not to sell certain books.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:41.187
They threatened my children’s future

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:43.272
if I did it again.

00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:48.694
How did you financially prepare for this?

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:55.284
We had to sell our house and car.

00:08:55.284 --> 00:08:57.787
But we also knew that by selling at that time,

00:08:57.787 --> 00:09:01.040
we had to sell low.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.627
It barely covered the travel expenses.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:09.382
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;The migrants then took long-distance buses&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.050
&lt;i&gt;to a small town in Colombia near&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.177
&lt;i&gt;the border with Panama,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:13.177 --> 00:09:16.472
&lt;i&gt;across the sea from the Darién Gap,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:16.472 --> 00:09:17.390
&lt;i&gt;Necoclí.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.480
&lt;i&gt;Mr. Li had been so full of confidence,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.275
&lt;i&gt;but texted me in the evening,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:30.570
&lt;i&gt;hoping that we would pick him up&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at the station in Necoclí.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.364
&lt;i&gt;The message ended with&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;two "scared" emojis.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:36.617
[Mr. Li] &lt;i&gt;These four days&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:36.617 --> 00:09:39.161
&lt;i&gt;have felt like traveling halfway across China.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:39.161 --> 00:09:41.581
&lt;i&gt;Sleeping on the coach at night.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:44.083
&lt;i&gt;It's so hard.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.424
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;The once quiet and peaceful town&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:53.843
&lt;i&gt;with a population of only 20,000&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:53.843 --> 00:09:56.137
&lt;i&gt;has become noisy and crowded&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;due to the influx&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:58.139
&lt;i&gt;of tens of thousands of migrants.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.391
&lt;i&gt;Merchants and shops no longer&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;target tourists&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:00.391 --> 00:10:02.852
&lt;i&gt;but instead are engaged&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in the immigration business.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:02.852 --> 00:10:04.520
&lt;i&gt;Prices are steadily rising,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.523
&lt;i&gt;with migrants sleeping in tents on the beach.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:07.523 --> 00:10:08.691
&lt;i&gt;But migrants from China&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:08.691 --> 00:10:11.110
&lt;i&gt;usually have enough money&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to stay in hotels.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.990
[Ferry announcement]

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:20.494
&lt;i&gt;As long as the wind and waves&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:20.494 --> 00:10:21.996
&lt;i&gt;are calm enough for travel,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:25.082
&lt;i&gt;hundreds of migrants will gather&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at the port before 8 a.m.,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:25.082 --> 00:10:27.251
&lt;i&gt;waiting to take a one-hour speedboat&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:27.251 --> 00:10:29.545
&lt;i&gt;to enter the Darién Gap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:35.926
Our company transports approximately

00:10:35.926 --> 00:10:37.678
600 to 700 people via ferry every day.

00:10:37.678 --> 00:10:45.686
Everyday there are about 100 to 120 Asians.

00:10:47.188 --> 00:10:50.066
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Between 2011 and 2021,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:50.066 --> 00:10:54.153
&lt;i&gt;only about 100 Chinese citizens&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;crossed the Darién Gap,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:55.946
&lt;i&gt;but in the second half of 2022,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:55.946 --> 00:10:57.365
&lt;i&gt;numbers began to surge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:57.365 --> 00:10:58.616
&lt;i&gt;In 2023,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:58.616 --> 00:11:01.160
&lt;i&gt;there were more than 25,000.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:02.286 --> 00:11:03.412
We left on March 10th.

00:11:03.412 --> 00:11:05.831
We bought our plane tickets early.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:06.707
The day before we left,

00:11:06.707 --> 00:11:08.584
my wife was still strongly against it,

00:11:08.584 --> 00:11:10.628
but I told her that we had to leave.

00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:13.547
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Ding owned a company in Shandong&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:13.547 --> 00:11:15.049
&lt;i&gt;and owns a house and car.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:15.049 --> 00:11:17.426
&lt;i&gt;He is considered middle class in China.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:17.426 --> 00:11:19.303
A large part of this is for my children.

00:11:20.137 --> 00:11:23.349
Because we lived in a small town,

00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:26.936
educational resources are very limited.

00:11:26.936 --> 00:11:29.271
If you want to provide your children
with better educational resources,

00:11:29.271 --> 00:11:32.441
you have to spend a lot of money
to buy a house in a big city,

00:11:32.441 --> 00:11:35.069
but that amount of money is hard to make.

00:11:35.069 --> 00:11:35.986
In the beginning,

00:11:35.986 --> 00:11:37.988
I was planning on immigrating
by studying abroad

00:11:37.988 --> 00:11:39.156
or even on a tourist visa,

00:11:39.156 --> 00:11:41.659
but it was simply impossible
for a family of three.

00:11:41.659 --> 00:11:42.743
How much this one?

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:46.372
Ok.

00:11:47.623 --> 00:11:49.709
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;As we wandered around Necoclí,&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:53.921
&lt;i&gt;we met some single women&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in their twenties and early thirties,&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:53.921 --> 00:11:56.465
&lt;i&gt;Cindy was the only one&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;willing to be interviewed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:03.514 --> 00:12:04.390
How much?

00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:05.558
-Two people?
-Yeah.

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.226
Seventy-five.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.061
Seventy-five.

00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:10.688
Including this?

00:12:10.688 --> 00:12:11.522
Yes.

00:12:13.566 --> 00:12:14.692
One, two, three.

00:12:14.692 --> 00:12:15.693
Seventy-five.

00:12:16.193 --> 00:12:17.027
Ok?

00:12:17.027 --> 00:12:19.155
Have nice one, strong one.

00:12:22.491 --> 00:12:24.201
Ok, let me think first.

00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:31.041
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Cindy is from Fujian.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:31.041 --> 00:12:32.543
&lt;i&gt;Thirty years ago,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:32.543 --> 00:12:35.379
&lt;i&gt;people from Fuzhou made the dangerous attempt&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to cross the Pacific&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:35.379 --> 00:12:37.339
&lt;i&gt;and to come to the United States.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:37.339 --> 00:12:39.967
&lt;i&gt;The case of the "Golden Venture" shocked society.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:40.676 --> 00:12:42.219
&lt;i&gt;Thirty years later,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:42.219 --> 00:12:44.764
&lt;i&gt;young women like Cindy &lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;who can speak English&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:47.391
&lt;i&gt;and even worked in South Africa,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:47.391 --> 00:12:49.226
&lt;i&gt;have also become migrants.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:50.144 --> 00:12:53.397
&lt;i&gt;She originally applied for&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;an Ecuadorian business visa&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:53.397 --> 00:12:55.983
&lt;i&gt;but waited in vain for several months.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:55.983 --> 00:13:00.237
&lt;i&gt;She met a group of young women&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;about her age in Necoclí&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:00.237 --> 00:13:01.781
&lt;i&gt;and joined them.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:06.035
When did you decide?

00:13:06.744 --> 00:13:10.080
To take this path?

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.207
Just a few days ago.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:13.667
The day before yesterday.

00:13:13.667 --> 00:13:14.794
I couldn’t drag on any longer.

00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:16.420
If it kept dragging on,

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.463
I’m stuck in the same place.

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.632
I might as well take another path,

00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:21.133
it may not be as good,

00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:23.761
but it’s a way to move forward.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.991
[Alicia] You found a random hotel online, right?

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:48.953
[Mr. Li] And I couldn’t find one,
so I just picked this one.

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:58.087
How much is 120,000?

00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:03.259
Thirty dollars?

00:14:03.259 --> 00:14:04.593
[Alicia] Right, around that.

00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:08.806
Any discount for staying two nights?

00:14:40.421 --> 00:14:45.175
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;We met three young men&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at a fried chicken restaurant,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:45.175 --> 00:14:47.678
&lt;i&gt;two of whom were a gay couple.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:50.639 --> 00:14:55.019
&lt;i&gt;Lee and Ivan are from Sichuan and Guizhou,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:55.019 --> 00:14:57.646
&lt;i&gt;have been together for more than four years.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:57.646 --> 00:15:00.774
&lt;i&gt;They ran a coffee shop together in China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:00.774 --> 00:15:03.944
&lt;i&gt;lived a fulfilling life and traveled frequently.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:03.944 --> 00:15:05.738
&lt;i&gt;But just because they are gay,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:05.738 --> 00:15:09.241
&lt;i&gt;they once found themselves in trouble&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;with the Chinese police.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:09.241 --> 00:15:10.200
[Lee] &lt;i&gt;We booked a room &lt;/i&gt;

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.493
&lt;i&gt;with one bed in Shanghai&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:13.662
&lt;i&gt;The police showed up in 10 minutes，&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:13.662 --> 00:15:15.998
asking &lt;i&gt;"Why are you two sleeping in one bed?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:15.998 --> 00:15:17.750
&lt;i&gt;Are you taking illegal drugs?"&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.376
&lt;i&gt;Usually two men will book&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:19.376 --> 00:15:21.462
&lt;i&gt;one room with two beds.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:22.504 --> 00:15:25.132
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;They were envious of same-sex marriage&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;legalization in Taiwan,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:25.132 --> 00:15:27.718
&lt;i&gt;and lamented that &lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;after Xi Jinping came to power,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:27.718 --> 00:15:31.263
&lt;i&gt;there was even a crackdown on&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;LGBTQ+ dating apps.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:31.931 --> 00:15:34.767
[Lee] We can’t get legally married in China.

00:15:34.767 --> 00:15:36.644
In Taiwan, it’s possible.

00:15:36.644 --> 00:15:38.312
Yes, (same-sex) marriage was legalized

00:15:38.312 --> 00:15:40.230
in Taiwan in 2019.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.815
[Ivan] I’m so jealous.

00:15:42.358 --> 00:15:45.486
[Lee] We’re planning for the future.

00:15:45.653 --> 00:15:47.529
In China, we can’t get married, have children,

00:15:47.529 --> 00:15:49.531
have surrogates, or adopt.

00:15:49.531 --> 00:15:52.201
There are no guarantees in our later years.

00:15:52.201 --> 00:15:53.702
China does not have a safety net for us,

00:15:53.702 --> 00:15:54.745
like medical coverage.

00:15:54.745 --> 00:15:55.955
When we are old，

00:15:55.955 --> 00:15:58.290
we will have no families.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.834
We can easily see what life would be like

00:16:00.834 --> 00:16:03.295
for elderly gay men in China,

00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:05.714
what our situation would look like,

00:16:05.714 --> 00:16:08.092
so we decided to leave.

00:16:13.681 --> 00:16:15.140
I'll grab something to eat first...

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:19.353
[Alicia] We’ve eaten there before.

00:16:21.188 --> 00:16:23.565
How do you say “the Statue of Liberty”
in English?

00:16:24.274 --> 00:16:26.276
[Alicia] The Statue of Liberty.

00:16:26.527 --> 00:16:29.780
The Statue of Liberty was calling to me
a few months ago.

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.412
[Cindy] &lt;i&gt;I had fears and worries before I left,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:36.412 --> 00:16:37.329
&lt;i&gt;but after departing,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:37.329 --> 00:16:39.581
&lt;i&gt;I felt those fears and worries no longer existed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:39.581 --> 00:16:40.958
&lt;i&gt;Because you are already on the road,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:40.958 --> 00:16:42.543
&lt;i&gt;all you need to do&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:42.543 --> 00:16:45.087
&lt;i&gt;is to think about how to take each next step.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.882
[Mr. Li] &lt;i&gt;Life has infinite possibilities&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:48.882 --> 00:16:50.509
&lt;i&gt;as long as you don’t give up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:51.552 --> 00:16:54.972
[Cindy] &lt;i&gt;If you treat this process as&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;a kind of journey,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:54.972 --> 00:16:56.807
&lt;i&gt;it won’t feel so oppressive,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:56.807 --> 00:16:57.725
&lt;i&gt;it will be much better.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:59.351 --> 00:17:01.854
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Most Chinese people choose the Carretto route,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:04.398
&lt;i&gt;allowing them to cross the rainforests&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt; in just two days.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:04.398 --> 00:17:08.610
&lt;i&gt;But the smugglers worried that filming&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;would affect their business,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.530
&lt;i&gt;and warned us to stay away.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:15.284
&lt;i&gt;For safety reasons, we chose the Acandí route,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:15.284 --> 00:17:17.494
&lt;i&gt;which takes three to five days.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:25.127 --> 00:17:27.254
&lt;i&gt;A motorcycle convoy took us and our guide&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:27.254 --> 00:17:28.797
&lt;i&gt;to the entrance of the rainforest.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:32.134 --> 00:17:34.219
&lt;i&gt;The campground is far away&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;from roads and ports,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:36.096
&lt;i&gt;but provides hot food, a grocery store,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:36.096 --> 00:17:38.057
&lt;i&gt;and even Wi-Fi.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:38.849 --> 00:17:41.518
&lt;i&gt;The armed militia organization&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;that controls this place&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:41.518 --> 00:17:44.396
&lt;i&gt;requires migrants to pay&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;a so-called "management fee,"&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:47.441
&lt;i&gt;which varies from tens to hundreds&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;of US dollars.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:47.441 --> 00:17:48.817
&lt;i&gt;After paying the fee,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:48.817 --> 00:17:51.570
&lt;i&gt;migrants receive a fluorescent wristband.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:52.154 --> 00:17:54.573
&lt;i&gt;The primitive rainforest is like a nightclub,&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:54.573 --> 00:17:56.241
&lt;i&gt;which can only be entered with a wristband.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:57.534 --> 00:18:00.496
&lt;i&gt;The business of facilitating smuggling&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;migrants may not be legal,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:00.496 --> 00:18:02.998
&lt;i&gt;but it is estimated to be quite profitable.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:04.208 --> 00:18:06.585
&lt;i&gt;Mantinaz is the camp manager,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:08.754
&lt;i&gt;managing a team of more than 200 people.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:09.213 --> 00:18:11.256
[Camp Manager] It’s not a business.

00:18:11.256 --> 00:18:14.843
It’s a service, and they sincerely thank us.

00:18:14.843 --> 00:18:20.349
That’s why people who pass through
tell others to follow,

00:18:20.349 --> 00:18:24.770
because the most important thing is

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:27.064
that we integrate transport

00:18:27.064 --> 00:18:28.732
and a place to sleep.

00:18:28.732 --> 00:18:32.152
These places are all private property
and belong to the indigenous people.

00:18:32.152 --> 00:18:33.403
Of course, they cannot be free.

00:18:34.113 --> 00:18:38.742
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;We met two Chinese families&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and several young people.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:38.742 --> 00:18:42.079
&lt;i&gt;Other migrants had an open attitude&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;towards the media,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:42.079 --> 00:18:45.791
&lt;i&gt;but Chinese migrants were worried&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for their families in China.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:47.543
&lt;i&gt;Some were even worried that&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:47.543 --> 00:18:50.129
&lt;i&gt;there were Chinese spies in their midst here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:50.129 --> 00:18:52.840
&lt;i&gt;Fortunately, one of them&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;was willing to accept our interview.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:59.054 --> 00:19:00.597
My name is Yu Chunfei.

00:19:00.597 --> 00:19:02.683
Born in 1984.

00:19:02.683 --> 00:19:05.227
I was born in Shanxi.

00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:07.146
After graduation

00:19:07.146 --> 00:19:08.605
I worked in property management in Beijing

00:19:08.605 --> 00:19:10.065
for about 10 years.

00:19:10.065 --> 00:19:12.359
I’ve also worked in some sales jobs.

00:19:12.776 --> 00:19:13.527
I had a family,

00:19:13.527 --> 00:19:14.903
but we are divorced.

00:19:14.903 --> 00:19:16.405
My son is almost five years old.

00:19:16.405 --> 00:19:17.531
He lives with my ex-wife.

00:19:17.531 --> 00:19:19.616
My ex-wife works

00:19:20.826 --> 00:19:22.870
in a state-owned enterprise.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.955
She is very…

00:19:25.789 --> 00:19:27.207
nationalistic, you know,

00:19:27.207 --> 00:19:29.918
and we had little in common.

00:19:32.796 --> 00:19:37.384
After leaving China and traveling all over,

00:19:37.384 --> 00:19:39.595
I found I wasn’t as stressed.

00:19:39.595 --> 00:19:41.013
I’m so happy.

00:19:41.013 --> 00:19:42.931
I posted several WeChat moments,

00:19:42.931 --> 00:19:44.766
and many people said I gained weight.

00:19:44.766 --> 00:19:46.476
I said I ate too well.

00:19:48.937 --> 00:19:50.480
We have to travel for four days,

00:19:51.648 --> 00:19:53.609
so we have to bring enough food.

00:19:57.029 --> 00:19:58.822
Bread is squashed like this.

00:19:58.822 --> 00:19:59.948
Easy to pack.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.579
I packed some eggs in the morning.

00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:09.082
But I drank a little wine at night and fell asleep,

00:20:09.082 --> 00:20:11.043
and now the eggs are all crushed.

00:20:11.043 --> 00:20:13.045
A sticky mess now.

00:20:13.045 --> 00:20:15.047
Because of the Communist Party,

00:20:15.047 --> 00:20:18.175
China gives the world the impression 
of producing garbage.

00:20:18.175 --> 00:20:18.967
Look at this bag,

00:20:18.967 --> 00:20:20.719
I just carried it for only a few days,

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.847
and it's already broken.

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:27.184
Someone punched a hole for me

00:20:27.184 --> 00:20:29.394
with a knife and tied a knot.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.313
This bag is useless.

00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:33.398
Fortunately, I didn't throw away the other bag.

00:20:40.614 --> 00:20:42.574
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;It’s almost pitch black in the rainforest&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:42.574 --> 00:20:44.284
&lt;i&gt;after 6:30 p.m.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.662
&lt;i&gt;Early the next morning,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:46.662 --> 00:20:49.373
&lt;i&gt;the migrants gathered&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at the wooden gate of the camp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:49.373 --> 00:20:52.292
&lt;i&gt;A man spoke with a megaphone,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:52.292 --> 00:20:54.670
&lt;i&gt;as if at a pep rally before a marathon.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:56.046 --> 00:20:57.881
We are all the same.

00:20:58.257 --> 00:20:59.549
We must support each other.

00:20:59.549 --> 00:21:00.926
Don't be rude.

00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:02.928
We are all equal.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:06.890
No one is more important than anyone else.

00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:11.436
You spent money.

00:21:11.979 --> 00:21:13.897
Today we must do things right.

00:21:13.897 --> 00:21:15.190
Are you ready?

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.316
Yes.

00:21:19.486 --> 00:21:21.613
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;There was no shot from a starting gun,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:21.613 --> 00:21:23.865
&lt;i&gt;just the door of the camp&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;squeezed open by the crowd.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:24.366 --> 00:21:27.244
&lt;i&gt;And we followed Yu Chunfei&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:27.244 --> 00:21:29.579
&lt;i&gt;and hundreds of migrants&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:29.579 --> 00:21:32.791
&lt;i&gt;As they officially entered the Darién Gap,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:32.791 --> 00:21:34.209
&lt;i&gt;which is 100 kilometers long,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:34.209 --> 00:21:36.586
&lt;i&gt;has no roads, and is full of danger.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:39.006 --> 00:21:40.549
&lt;i&gt;In 2023,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:40.549 --> 00:21:43.135
&lt;i&gt;520,000 people crossed the Darién Gap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.305
&lt;i&gt;They mainly came from Central&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and South American countries,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:49.308
&lt;i&gt;but many also came from Africa and Asia.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:49.933 --> 00:21:51.393
&lt;i&gt;As of January this year,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:51.393 --> 00:21:54.313
&lt;i&gt;the number of Chinese migrants&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;surpassed those from Ecuador,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:54.313 --> 00:21:55.105
&lt;i&gt;ranking only behind Venezuelan&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:55.939
&lt;i&gt;ranking only behind Venezuelan&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:55.939 --> 00:21:57.524
&lt;i&gt;and Haitian migrants.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:58.191 --> 00:21:59.735
&lt;i&gt;Chinese migrants&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:59.735 --> 00:22:01.236
&lt;i&gt;are the largest migrant group&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:01.236 --> 00:22:02.863
&lt;i&gt;besides Latin Americans.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:07.784 --> 00:22:09.328
I should have brought my son.

00:22:09.328 --> 00:22:12.706
Everyone's physical strength is different,

00:22:12.706 --> 00:22:15.000
and walking on this kind of trail
is quite familiar to me.

00:22:16.585 --> 00:22:17.627
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;On the first day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:17.627 --> 00:22:20.213
&lt;i&gt;perhaps propped up by adrenaline,&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:20.213 --> 00:22:23.383
&lt;i&gt;Everyone said it was easier than expected, &lt;/i&gt;

00:22:23.383 --> 00:22:25.010
&lt;i&gt;talking and laughing along the way.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.679
&lt;i&gt;Many people also enthusiastically&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;took photos with Yu Chunfei.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:27.971 --> 00:22:29.389
Venezuela and China.

00:22:29.848 --> 00:22:30.640
Yeah.

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:32.142
China and Venezuela

00:22:32.142 --> 00:22:32.934
To the whole world!

00:22:35.312 --> 00:22:36.772
What did he say?

00:22:36.772 --> 00:22:41.276
He said Venezuelans and Chinese
go everywhere in the world.

00:22:43.153 --> 00:22:44.988
&lt;i&gt;[Alicia] We happened to&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;meet the Venezuelan&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:44.988 --> 00:22:47.741
&lt;i&gt;who helped him buy&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the fluorescent wristband.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:47.741 --> 00:22:50.410
&lt;i&gt;He resold it to Yu Chunfei for 70 US dollars.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:53.747
&lt;i&gt;If Yu Chunfei had bought it himself&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;from the smugglers,&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:53.747 --> 00:22:55.874
&lt;i&gt;he would have paid 350 dollars.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:55.874 --> 00:22:59.336
People from many countries come here.

00:22:59.336 --> 00:23:00.879
They pass through the Darién Gap.

00:23:00.879 --> 00:23:03.882
I don’t know what is happening in China now.

00:23:03.882 --> 00:23:05.634
Many Chinese are coming here.

00:23:05.634 --> 00:23:07.719
[Mr. Li] &lt;i&gt;This is the second big mountain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:08.637 --> 00:23:10.389
&lt;i&gt;Follow the guide.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:13.642
[Ding’s wife] &lt;i&gt;Just hold onto daddy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:13.642 --> 00:23:14.851
&lt;i&gt;Don’t worry.  Sleep.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:16.186 --> 00:23:17.813
I don’t know what’s going on.

00:23:18.647 --> 00:23:20.941
Before, there were virtually no Chinese.

00:23:20.941 --> 00:23:24.403
Now many Chinese come.

00:23:24.403 --> 00:23:25.237
A large number.

00:23:41.169 --> 00:23:44.506
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;We followed Yu Chunfei&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to the next camp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:44.506 --> 00:23:47.509
&lt;i&gt;The smell was terrible in the rainforest,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:47.509 --> 00:23:49.010
&lt;i&gt;a mixed smell of feces, urine,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.054
&lt;i&gt;and decay.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:51.054 --> 00:23:52.889
&lt;i&gt;In the garbage dumps,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:52.889 --> 00:23:56.643
&lt;i&gt;there are many with Simplified Chinese.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:05.402 --> 00:24:07.487
During the three years of the epidemic,

00:24:07.487 --> 00:24:09.823
my overall mental health was very bad.

00:24:09.823 --> 00:24:13.368
I was in constant fear.

00:24:16.496 --> 00:24:18.290
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Yu Chunfei showed me&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:20.417
&lt;i&gt;a stack of documents he had prepared&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:20.417 --> 00:24:22.127
&lt;i&gt;to apply for asylum in the United States.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:22.127 --> 00:24:23.336
&lt;i&gt;He refused to get vaccinated&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:23.336 --> 00:24:25.172
&lt;i&gt;during the epidemic,&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:25.172 --> 00:24:27.757
&lt;i&gt;because he doubted the safety&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;of Chinese vaccines.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:28.467 --> 00:24:29.718
&lt;i&gt;But this decision&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:29.718 --> 00:24:31.428
&lt;i&gt;cost him his job&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:31.428 --> 00:24:32.429
&lt;i&gt;and left him living on the streets.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:34.598
Your employer would force you
to get vaccinated.

00:24:34.598 --> 00:24:36.349
Otherwise, you’d be fired.

00:24:37.017 --> 00:24:38.059
I rented an apartment.

00:24:38.059 --> 00:24:40.687
Then the neighborhood committee
harassed my landlord

00:24:40.687 --> 00:24:41.646
to get me vaccinated.

00:24:42.314 --> 00:24:43.815
Tenants must be vaccinated.

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:46.359
Then my landlord came to persuade me.

00:24:47.068 --> 00:24:48.695
So I couldn't even find a place to live.

00:24:49.196 --> 00:24:50.155
I couldn't find a job.

00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:51.406
Then there was a really tough time

00:24:51.406 --> 00:24:52.699
when I couldn’t even rent a place.

00:24:53.366 --> 00:24:55.452
So after thinking about it,

00:24:55.452 --> 00:24:56.411
I bought a van.

00:24:56.411 --> 00:24:58.371
I slept in the van, parked on the street.

00:24:58.371 --> 00:25:00.373
That way, I wouldn't be locked down

00:25:00.373 --> 00:25:01.374
in a residential compound.

00:25:03.001 --> 00:25:05.045
&lt;i&gt;[Alicia] Because of this, Yu Chunfei spent a year&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:05.045 --> 00:25:06.046
&lt;i&gt;in the van.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:06.588 --> 00:25:08.548
&lt;i&gt;He thought that faking an allergy to proteins&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:08.548 --> 00:25:10.383
&lt;i&gt;could help him avoid forced vaccination.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:10.383 --> 00:25:12.719
&lt;i&gt;So he came up with an idea&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:12.719 --> 00:25:14.596
&lt;i&gt;to have doctors write a note for him.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:15.222 --> 00:25:16.973
I thought about it for several days,

00:25:17.474 --> 00:25:18.475
and I came up with a solution.

00:25:19.226 --> 00:25:21.853
I rubbed peach fuzz all over my body.

00:25:22.604 --> 00:25:26.483
And broke out in a rash,

00:25:26.483 --> 00:25:27.651
and then I went to see the doctor.

00:25:27.651 --> 00:25:30.612
I said, I’m allergic to eggs.

00:25:30.612 --> 00:25:32.364
I had a rash all over.

00:25:34.157 --> 00:25:35.492
I didn't have a choice.

00:25:37.035 --> 00:25:39.621
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;After a resting for a night in camp,&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:39.621 --> 00:25:42.290
&lt;i&gt;we headed the next day to the border&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:42.290 --> 00:25:43.542
&lt;i&gt;of Colombia and Panama.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:48.713 --> 00:25:51.716
I saw dogs walking along the way.

00:25:52.509 --> 00:25:53.468
Dogs have no nationality.

00:25:53.468 --> 00:25:54.636
They can go anywhere,

00:25:54.636 --> 00:25:56.471
I should be able to, with some efforts.

00:26:03.186 --> 00:26:05.105
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Before crossing the border,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:05.105 --> 00:26:08.984
&lt;i&gt;the paid helpers who carried migrants'&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;luggage and children&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:08.984 --> 00:26:12.445
&lt;i&gt;left as if they were clocking off of work.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:12.445 --> 00:26:15.031
&lt;i&gt;This also meant that the migrants had to&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:15.031 --> 00:26:17.075
&lt;i&gt;rely on themselves&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for the rest of the journey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:36.428 --> 00:26:39.139
&lt;i&gt;This was our second day in the Darién Gap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:39.139 --> 00:26:42.392
&lt;i&gt;There was not as much shade as we imagined.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:42.392 --> 00:26:45.437
&lt;i&gt;We walked from 6 a.m. to 3 or 4 p.m.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:45.437 --> 00:26:47.397
&lt;i&gt;under the scorching sun&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:47.397 --> 00:26:50.025
&lt;i&gt;and had to constantly&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;wade through the water.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:50.025 --> 00:26:52.152
&lt;i&gt;Everyone talked less&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:52.152 --> 00:26:54.696
&lt;i&gt;and began feeling the difficulty&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;of the journey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:58.617 --> 00:27:01.286
&lt;i&gt;Although we were walking along a river,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:01.286 --> 00:27:03.747
&lt;i&gt;drinking unfiltered water can easily&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:03.747 --> 00:27:06.207
&lt;i&gt;lead to vomiting, diarrhea, or illness&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:06.207 --> 00:27:07.876
&lt;i&gt;due to bacterial contaminants.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:07.876 --> 00:27:09.377
This water tastes really good.

00:27:27.395 --> 00:27:28.647
&lt;i&gt;That night,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:28.647 --> 00:27:30.982
&lt;i&gt;there was a heavy downpour.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:30.982 --> 00:27:34.277
&lt;i&gt;Yu Chunfei’s tent was completely soaked.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:34.277 --> 00:27:36.404
&lt;i&gt;He kept waving his cellphone flashlight&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:36.404 --> 00:27:38.031
&lt;i&gt;in his tent.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:39.574 --> 00:27:43.119
&lt;i&gt;I had heard that people can&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;suffer from hypothermia in heavy rains.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:43.119 --> 00:27:45.664
&lt;i&gt;I called him to take shelter&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;under my rain cover,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:45.664 --> 00:27:47.624
&lt;i&gt;but he didn’t respond.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:47.624 --> 00:27:52.420
&lt;i&gt;The next day he woke up with a bad cold.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:56.841 --> 00:27:59.302
[Cindy] &lt;i&gt;Here, I have faith that&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:59.302 --> 00:28:01.054
&lt;i&gt;I will make it out,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:01.054 --> 00:28:02.847
&lt;i&gt;it’s just a matter of time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:02.847 --> 00:28:04.557
[man 6] &lt;i&gt;Every step I take&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:04.557 --> 00:28:07.519
&lt;i&gt;brings me closer to the camp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:07.519 --> 00:28:09.938
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;No one can stop me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:22.617 --> 00:28:23.660
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; On the third day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:26.121
&lt;i&gt;Yu Chunfei walked out of our sight&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;several times&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:26.121 --> 00:28:27.831
&lt;i&gt;because he was rushing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:29.708 --> 00:28:32.585
&lt;i&gt;The ground was slippery and muddy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:32.585 --> 00:28:35.797
&lt;i&gt;Yu Chunfei fell several times along the way.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:35.797 --> 00:28:38.591
&lt;i&gt;Once, he fell directly from a two-story rock wall&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:38.591 --> 00:28:40.343
&lt;i&gt;into the river valley,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:40.343 --> 00:28:42.762
&lt;i&gt;scraping up his whole body.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:42.762 --> 00:28:44.681
&lt;i&gt;There were no first aid facilities&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:44.681 --> 00:28:46.516
&lt;i&gt;or emergency medical stations,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:46.516 --> 00:28:48.393
&lt;i&gt;and everyone was too busy&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;taking care of themselves.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:48.393 --> 00:28:50.395
&lt;i&gt;If someone was left behind due to injury,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:50.395 --> 00:28:52.522
&lt;i&gt;the consequences are difficult to imagine.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:55.233 --> 00:28:58.862
&lt;i&gt;We saw three dead bodies in one day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:59.779 --> 00:29:01.030
&lt;i&gt;one of which was a woman&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:01.030 --> 00:29:03.032
&lt;i&gt;abandoned along the roadside.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:09.789 --> 00:29:12.208
She was alone,

00:29:12.208 --> 00:29:14.127
her companions had left her behind.

00:29:15.670 --> 00:29:17.130
That's the way it is here.

00:29:17.130 --> 00:29:19.007
You have to take care of yourself first.

00:29:21.968 --> 00:29:25.013
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; A Venezuelan migrant picked up a bone&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;from one of the corpses&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:25.013 --> 00:29:26.931
&lt;i&gt;and said he would take it with him&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:28.808
&lt;i&gt;to the United States.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:45.784 --> 00:29:47.994
&lt;i&gt;When we arrived at the camp on the third day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:47.994 --> 00:29:49.662
&lt;i&gt;we learned that the night before,&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:49.662 --> 00:29:51.080
&lt;i&gt;migrants had been robbed&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:53.166
&lt;i&gt;and attacked near the camp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:53.833 --> 00:29:55.376
&lt;i&gt;There was even a shootout&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:55.376 --> 00:29:56.961
&lt;i&gt;between the robbers and the Panama&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;border control.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:57.754 --> 00:29:58.963
&lt;i&gt;The next morning,&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:58.963 --> 00:30:00.840
&lt;i&gt;we had barely rested&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:00.840 --> 00:30:02.342
&lt;i&gt;and just wanted to leave the jungle&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:02.342 --> 00:30:03.426
&lt;i&gt;as soon as possible.&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:22.445 --> 00:30:23.822
Get on the boat.

00:30:51.975 --> 00:30:53.434
There must be quite a lot of Chinese here.

00:30:53.434 --> 00:30:55.645
When they see me, they say “Chino, Chino.”

00:31:07.782 --> 00:31:09.909
[Yu] &lt;i&gt;I had never cast a vote in all my life.&lt;/i&gt;

00:31:09.909 --> 00:31:13.288
&lt;i&gt;This time I voted with my feet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:31:18.251 --> 00:31:19.711
[Alicia] What do you think you are voting for

00:31:19.711 --> 00:31:21.004
with your feet on this journey?

00:31:22.297 --> 00:31:25.592
I vote for having no fear.

00:31:26.801 --> 00:31:28.761
To get rid of that feeling of fear,

00:31:28.761 --> 00:31:30.680
to break away from fear.

00:31:32.390 --> 00:31:34.767
I lived in fear every day.

00:31:34.767 --> 00:31:36.686
Fear of being arrested for talking,

00:31:36.686 --> 00:31:38.479
or for doing something.

00:31:38.479 --> 00:31:41.649
Inexplicable panic and nervousness.

00:31:41.649 --> 00:31:43.026
This is what I am voting for.

00:31:48.948 --> 00:31:51.284
[Alicia] We’re here, finally here!

00:31:51.284 --> 00:31:52.410
We are here.

00:31:54.454 --> 00:31:55.997
[Alicia] Are you happy?

00:31:58.750 --> 00:31:59.834
[Yu] Tired.

00:31:59.834 --> 00:32:00.960
But I am very happy.

00:32:07.550 --> 00:32:09.677
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;As the boat docked,&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:09.677 --> 00:32:11.638
&lt;i&gt;we finally walked out of the jungle.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:20.063 --> 00:32:21.522
[Man 7] Coming out of the Darién Gap,

00:32:21.522 --> 00:32:22.565
I saw cars and felt that

00:32:22.565 --> 00:32:26.277
we had returned to a more modern era.

00:32:27.153 --> 00:32:30.782
I feel like it’s finally come to an end.

00:32:30.782 --> 00:32:34.160
I just want to eat
a chicken drumstick over rice,

00:32:34.160 --> 00:32:36.204
drink a can of Coke,

00:32:36.204 --> 00:32:38.247
and then go to sleep.

00:32:39.374 --> 00:32:40.833
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;After leaving the Darién Gap,&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:40.833 --> 00:32:43.753
&lt;i&gt;the Panama border security&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:43.753 --> 00:32:47.173
&lt;i&gt;takes the migrants to camps&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;near the rainforest.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:47.173 --> 00:32:49.968
&lt;i&gt;International humanitarian organizations&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;are stationed in the camp,&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:49.968 --> 00:32:52.679
&lt;i&gt;providing free medical care, food,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and accommodation.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:52.679 --> 00:32:55.473
&lt;i&gt;Chinese migrants also call it a “refugee camp.”&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:58.309 --> 00:33:01.396
&lt;i&gt;There were around 200 migrants&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in camp that day.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:01.396 --> 00:33:03.231
&lt;i&gt;The soldiers on duty told us&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:03.231 --> 00:33:05.984
&lt;i&gt;that there were 69 Chinese among them,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:05.984 --> 00:33:07.485
&lt;i&gt;including a 12-year-old girl&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:07.485 --> 00:33:09.320
&lt;i&gt;who had been separated from her parents.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:11.698 --> 00:33:14.200
&lt;i&gt;He came from Urumqi, Xinjiang.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:16.119
&lt;i&gt;His entire arm was severely sunburned&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:16.119 --> 00:33:18.287
&lt;i&gt;from walking through the rainforest.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:18.287 --> 00:33:21.332
&lt;i&gt;On November 24th, 2022,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:21.332 --> 00:33:23.626
&lt;i&gt;a fire broke out in Urumqi,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:23.626 --> 00:33:25.294
&lt;i&gt;triggering the "White Paper Movement"&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:25.294 --> 00:33:27.005
&lt;i&gt;against the government all over the country.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:27.005 --> 00:33:30.049
&lt;i&gt;This also became the catalyst&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for him to flee the country.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:30.049 --> 00:33:32.010
[man from Xinjiang] You see more and more

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:35.471
Chinese migrants in South America.

00:33:35.471 --> 00:33:37.056
Let me tell you,

00:33:37.056 --> 00:33:39.851
it is the Zero-Covid Policy that created
Chinese refugees.

00:33:40.768 --> 00:33:42.478
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Another family of four,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:42.478 --> 00:33:45.064
&lt;i&gt;the youngest child only six months old.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:45.064 --> 00:33:47.775
&lt;i&gt;This father has his own e-commerce business&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:47.775 --> 00:33:49.027
&lt;i&gt;and factory in China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:49.027 --> 00:33:50.737
&lt;i&gt;but for his children's future,&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:50.737 --> 00:33:52.196
&lt;i&gt;he still chose to flee.&lt;/i&gt;

00:33:53.239 --> 00:33:55.950
I don’t want the next generation to be like me, with no choice.

00:33:58.453 --> 00:34:00.913
[Alicia] So it is mainly for the children’s education

00:34:03.249 --> 00:34:04.625
and future?

00:34:04.625 --> 00:34:05.334
Yes.

00:34:05.960 --> 00:34:08.171
Schools brainwash our kids.

00:34:08.171 --> 00:34:10.465
There is no proper education.

00:34:11.466 --> 00:34:14.218
When they were performing in kindergarten,

00:34:14.218 --> 00:34:15.720
the costumes had the words

00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:16.929
"explosive pack" written on them.

00:34:16.929 --> 00:34:18.014
[Alicia] What did it say?

00:34:18.014 --> 00:34:18.723
Explosive pack.

00:34:19.849 --> 00:34:20.892
An explosive pack,

00:34:20.892 --> 00:34:21.976
meant to blow up bunkers.

00:34:22.894 --> 00:34:24.020
[Alicia] What does that mean?

00:34:24.771 --> 00:34:27.065
Like a suicide bomb...

00:34:29.567 --> 00:34:34.572
For a new China, charge!

00:34:37.158 --> 00:34:38.868
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In Taiwanese textbooks,&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:38.868 --> 00:34:41.412
&lt;i&gt;this anecdote is not mentioned.&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:41.954 --> 00:34:44.248
&lt;i&gt;It turns out that this originated from the story&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:44.248 --> 00:34:45.583
&lt;i&gt;of a PLA soldier named Dong Cunrui.&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:46.334 --> 00:34:47.919
&lt;i&gt;During the civil war in China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:47.919 --> 00:34:50.129
&lt;i&gt;he held up explosive packs&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:50.505 --> 00:34:52.465
&lt;i&gt;to blow up the enemy's bunker&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:52.673 --> 00:34:54.342
&lt;i&gt;and martyred himself for communism.&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:54.634 --> 00:34:56.511
&lt;i&gt;Therefore, he was regarded as a hero&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:56.511 --> 00:34:57.637
&lt;i&gt;by the Chinese Communist Party.&lt;/i&gt;

00:34:58.471 --> 00:35:01.349
For a new China, charge!

00:35:03.476 --> 00:35:06.729
She had to perform this
in her kindergarten.

00:35:06.729 --> 00:35:08.106
It was so scary to watch.

00:35:09.774 --> 00:35:11.776
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In the "refugee camp",&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;you need to line up for everything,&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:11.776 --> 00:35:13.361
&lt;i&gt;including handing in your passport,&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:13.361 --> 00:35:14.987
&lt;i&gt;having your fingerprints taken,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and receiving meals.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:15.321 --> 00:35:16.781
&lt;i&gt;The final wait&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:16.948 --> 00:35:19.867
&lt;i&gt;is to get on a bus arranged by&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the Panamanian government.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:20.243 --> 00:35:22.829
&lt;i&gt;and head to the border near Costa Rica.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:23.788 --> 00:35:25.790
&lt;i&gt;Feng Lianjin is from Shandong.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:25.790 --> 00:35:27.583
&lt;i&gt;He has been waiting here for two days.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:28.209 --> 00:35:30.128
I am twenty-eight this year, born in 1995.

00:35:30.128 --> 00:35:32.004
I’m an only child.

00:35:32.088 --> 00:35:33.673
[Alicia] What did your parents say?

00:35:33.673 --> 00:35:35.091
Did they know you were leaving,

00:35:35.091 --> 00:35:36.884
or did you not tell them?

00:35:36.884 --> 00:35:37.885
I told them.

00:35:38.845 --> 00:35:40.179
I told them,

00:35:40.179 --> 00:35:41.764
and they definitely disagreed,

00:35:41.764 --> 00:35:43.224
strongly disagreed.

00:35:43.224 --> 00:35:47.687
But I told them that I had made up my mind.

00:35:47.687 --> 00:35:50.731
If I really want to leave,
you can't stop me.

00:35:50.731 --> 00:35:54.861
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;They still have a long way to go.&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:54.861 --> 00:35:56.571
&lt;i&gt;Passing through Costa Rica,&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:56.821 --> 00:35:57.905
&lt;i&gt;Nicaragua,&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:58.156 --> 00:35:59.198
&lt;i&gt;Honduras,&lt;/i&gt;

00:35:59.407 --> 00:36:00.366
&lt;i&gt;and Guatemala,&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:00.867 --> 00:36:03.327
&lt;i&gt;they constantly switched between buses,&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:03.327 --> 00:36:05.580
&lt;i&gt;mini buses, and private cars,&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:05.580 --> 00:36:07.540
&lt;i&gt;covering more than 2,000 kilometers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:09.709
&lt;i&gt;Along the way, they might be solicited for money&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:09.709 --> 00:36:10.960
&lt;i&gt;by gangsters or police officers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:13.379 --> 00:36:14.881
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;That’s Mexico over there.&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:24.765 --> 00:36:26.184
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;About ten days later,&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:26.184 --> 00:36:30.646
&lt;i&gt;Yu Chunfei and Ding’s family&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;took a rubber raft&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:30.646 --> 00:36:32.899
&lt;i&gt;across the Suchiate River&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:32.899 --> 00:36:35.651
&lt;i&gt;and arrived at the border of&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Guatemala and Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:38.321 --> 00:36:40.323
&lt;i&gt;There are also people like Feng Lianjin&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:40.323 --> 00:36:42.575
&lt;i&gt;who squeezed into a truck&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;with a group of migrants&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:42.575 --> 00:36:43.784
&lt;i&gt;and entered Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:31.332
You know the route already,

00:37:31.332 --> 00:37:34.877
you can work as a smuggler, too.

00:37:36.212 --> 00:37:38.839
Ten thousand US dollars a day.

00:37:38.839 --> 00:37:40.424
Daily.

00:37:40.424 --> 00:37:42.218
Pure profit.

00:37:42.218 --> 00:37:44.679
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Feng Lianjin's estimation&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;is not an exaggeration.&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:44.679 --> 00:37:45.846
&lt;i&gt;Some Chinese people go through agencies&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:45.846 --> 00:37:48.057
&lt;i&gt;to apply for visas&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:48.057 --> 00:37:50.017
&lt;i&gt;and fly directly to Mexico,&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:50.017 --> 00:37:52.812
&lt;i&gt;Agencies offer all-inclusive packages&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;starting from 20,000 USD per person.&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:52.812 --> 00:37:53.980
&lt;i&gt;In comparison,&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:53.980 --> 00:37:55.564
&lt;i&gt;if you do it yourself&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:55.564 --> 00:37:57.316
&lt;i&gt;and rely on online guides,&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:57.316 --> 00:38:00.111
&lt;i&gt;each person will have to spend&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at least several thousand dollars.&lt;/i&gt;

00:38:01.362 --> 00:38:02.905
[Alicia] Your backpacks are so clean.

00:38:02.905 --> 00:38:04.156
You don’t look like someone

00:38:04.156 --> 00:38:06.033
who just walked through the Darién Gap

00:38:06.033 --> 00:38:07.493
[Lee] We washed them four times.

00:38:07.493 --> 00:38:09.620
Whenever we go to a place to wash clothes,

00:38:09.620 --> 00:38:11.747
if we have clothes to wash,
then we wash the backpacks.

00:38:11.747 --> 00:38:13.249
[Ivan] They’re quick-drying material.

00:38:17.336 --> 00:38:18.587
Bought in China.

00:38:18.587 --> 00:38:21.215
There are all kinds of
weird things available on Taobao.

00:38:27.179 --> 00:38:31.267
[Lee] Our essentials are battery banks.

00:38:31.267 --> 00:38:33.436
We make sure we have

00:38:33.436 --> 00:38:36.480
two battery banks at all times.

00:38:36.480 --> 00:38:38.399
Because no matter where you go,

00:38:38.399 --> 00:38:40.151
you have to make sure
that your cell phone has power.

00:38:40.151 --> 00:38:42.028
The most important things
are your passport and mobile phone.

00:38:44.322 --> 00:38:45.948
[Alicia] Two passports, easier for safekeeping

00:38:45.948 --> 00:38:47.616
[Lee] Yeah, we put them together.

00:38:50.494 --> 00:38:52.455
[Ding’s son] I want my mom.

00:38:55.333 --> 00:38:56.917
I want my mom.

00:38:59.545 --> 00:39:00.713
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;Along the way,&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:00.713 --> 00:39:02.631
&lt;i&gt;we threw away all the damaged&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;gear and clothes,&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:02.631 --> 00:39:04.216
&lt;i&gt;including shoes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:04.216 --> 00:39:07.845
&lt;i&gt;So, I want to buy us&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:07.845 --> 00:39:10.556
&lt;i&gt;some comfortable shoes and clothes&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:10.556 --> 00:39:12.266
&lt;i&gt;before leaving.&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:12.266 --> 00:39:15.269
&lt;i&gt;I want them to travel comfortably.&lt;/i&gt;

00:39:16.604 --> 00:39:19.023
[Alicia] Your little one walked over the first big mountain

00:39:19.023 --> 00:39:20.441
by himself.

00:39:20.441 --> 00:39:22.818
He probably had to go almost...

00:39:22.818 --> 00:39:24.987
five hours by himself.

00:39:26.405 --> 00:39:27.323
I didn’t want to,

00:39:27.323 --> 00:39:28.282
but had no choice.

00:39:28.282 --> 00:39:29.825
This is what we had to go through.

00:39:31.285 --> 00:39:33.329
[Alicia] You are also in Mexico now,

00:39:34.538 --> 00:39:36.207
and the next stop,
which is your destination,

00:39:36.207 --> 00:39:37.541
is just around the corner.

00:39:37.541 --> 00:39:40.044
How do you feel now?

00:39:43.005 --> 00:39:45.966
Maybe I won’t fully feel it

00:39:45.966 --> 00:39:48.344
until the last hurdle is crossed.

00:39:49.261 --> 00:39:51.180
Now I actually have to think about

00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:53.182
how to cross Tapachula.

00:39:53.808 --> 00:39:55.226
Everyone knows that Tapachula

00:39:55.226 --> 00:39:56.936
is quite difficult to get out of.

00:39:56.936 --> 00:39:58.646
Let’s wait until we get to Monterrey.

00:39:59.939 --> 00:40:02.858
[Alicia] How are you preparing to cross there?

00:40:03.484 --> 00:40:05.194
We’ll take a small car to cross there,

00:40:05.194 --> 00:40:07.196
and slowly bypass the checkpoint.

00:40:07.196 --> 00:40:08.280
That's the only way to go.

00:40:08.280 --> 00:40:10.574
I can't take a boat.

00:40:10.574 --> 00:40:11.617
I have a kid.

00:40:11.617 --> 00:40:13.077
It's just too dangerous.

00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:15.830
If it were just me,
it wouldn’t matter at all,

00:40:15.830 --> 00:40:16.997
but I have a kid and a family,

00:40:16.997 --> 00:40:17.998
so it's absolutely impossible.

00:40:21.043 --> 00:40:22.878
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Migrants take buses,&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:22.878 --> 00:40:25.464
&lt;i&gt;trains, and ride motorcycles,&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:25.464 --> 00:40:27.842
&lt;i&gt;trying to avoid dozens of checkpoints&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:27.842 --> 00:40:30.886
&lt;i&gt;designed to intercept them along the way.&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:30.886 --> 00:40:32.596
&lt;i&gt;The United States regularly pressures&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:32.596 --> 00:40:34.140
&lt;i&gt;the Mexican government to find ways&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:34.140 --> 00:40:37.518
&lt;i&gt;to stop migrants from heading north.&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:37.518 --> 00:40:39.937
&lt;i&gt;Taking a boat, as Ding said,&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:39.937 --> 00:40:41.480
&lt;i&gt;may be the most dangerous,&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:41.480 --> 00:40:45.234
&lt;i&gt;but fastest way to&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;get around these checkpoints.&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:45.234 --> 00:40:48.446
&lt;i&gt;Migrants take&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;a ten-hour overnight boat ride&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:48.446 --> 00:40:50.406
&lt;i&gt;from the port of Tapachula&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:52.366
&lt;i&gt;to the central city of Juchitán.&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:54.160 --> 00:40:56.370
&lt;i&gt;There are several Chinese restaurants&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in town&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:56.370 --> 00:40:58.914
&lt;i&gt;that also sell boat tickets.&lt;/i&gt;

00:40:58.914 --> 00:41:01.083
&lt;i&gt;One of the Chinese restaurant owners,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:01.083 --> 00:41:04.044
&lt;i&gt;charging 450 USD a ticket,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:04.044 --> 00:41:07.214
&lt;i&gt;kept emphasizing that&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the voyage was very safe.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:07.214 --> 00:41:08.507
&lt;i&gt;Trips are frequent.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:08.507 --> 00:41:11.093
&lt;i&gt;Smugglers would arrange same day departure&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:11.093 --> 00:41:12.720
&lt;i&gt;for ticket-holders.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:14.472 --> 00:41:16.056
[Xia Tian] &lt;i&gt;(We are) a family of three,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:16.056 --> 00:41:17.516
&lt;i&gt;and several men&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;suffered head injuries.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:17.558 --> 00:41:18.601
&lt;i&gt;They were held at gunpoint.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:19.143 --> 00:41:21.061
&lt;i&gt;The captain was severely beaten.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:21.729 --> 00:41:23.522
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;A mother nicknamed Xia Tian,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:23.522 --> 00:41:25.858
&lt;i&gt;her husband and son,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:25.858 --> 00:41:27.902
&lt;i&gt;and a group of other Chinese migrants&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:27.902 --> 00:41:31.405
&lt;i&gt;were attacked by bandits at sea.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:31.405 --> 00:41:33.824
&lt;i&gt;The captain suffered&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;a serious head injury,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:33.824 --> 00:41:35.534
&lt;i&gt;and most of the migrants' money&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:35.534 --> 00:41:36.452
&lt;i&gt;was taken.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:38.245 --> 00:41:39.330
[Xia Tian] &lt;i&gt;He searched me twice&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:40.206
&lt;i&gt;but didn't find my money.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:40.206 --> 00:41:41.999
&lt;i&gt;The third time, he found it&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:41.999 --> 00:41:43.292
&lt;i&gt;in my underwear.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:43.292 --> 00:41:44.293
&lt;i&gt;He even...&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:44.293 --> 00:41:47.630
&lt;i&gt;searched in my underwear&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:47.630 --> 00:41:48.464
&lt;i&gt;with his hand.&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:54.845 --> 00:41:56.347
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In March 2024,&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:56.347 --> 00:41:58.098
&lt;i&gt;a smuggler boat capsized&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:58.098 --> 00:42:00.476
&lt;i&gt;off the coast of southern Mexico,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:00.476 --> 00:42:02.144
&lt;i&gt;killing eight Chinese nationals,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:02.144 --> 00:42:03.896
&lt;i&gt;seven of whom were women.&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:15.741 --> 00:42:17.159
Because my foot was injured,

00:42:17.159 --> 00:42:18.577
I couldn't walk.

00:42:18.577 --> 00:42:19.787
For me,

00:42:19.787 --> 00:42:22.456
taking a boat made the most sense.

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:28.337
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;This man left his wife and son in China,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:28.337 --> 00:42:30.422
&lt;i&gt;walking the line alone.&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:30.422 --> 00:42:32.341
&lt;i&gt;When he was doing business&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in his hometown,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:32.341 --> 00:42:34.051
&lt;i&gt;he was blackmailed&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;by the local law enforcement.&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:34.051 --> 00:42:35.302
&lt;i&gt;He refused to cooperate,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:35.302 --> 00:42:37.221
&lt;i&gt;and they injured his lower back,&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:37.221 --> 00:42:40.015
&lt;i&gt;which indirectly caused him&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to walk with a limp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:42:41.809 --> 00:42:44.979
[man with foot injury] When I was on the boat,

00:42:44.979 --> 00:42:46.605
I don’t know why,

00:42:46.605 --> 00:42:49.650
but I felt really, really sad.

00:42:49.650 --> 00:42:51.610
I probably cried once on the boat.

00:42:51.610 --> 00:42:53.779
I was thinking about moving

00:42:53.779 --> 00:42:55.364
further away

00:42:58.450 --> 00:42:59.994
from my loved ones.

00:43:01.829 --> 00:43:04.957
Maybe we will never see
each other again

00:43:04.957 --> 00:43:06.166
in this life.

00:44:17.655 --> 00:44:19.198
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In mid-April,&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:19.198 --> 00:44:20.741
&lt;i&gt;the temperature in the southern Mexican city&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:20.741 --> 00:44:21.950
&lt;i&gt;of Arriaga&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:21.950 --> 00:44:23.952
&lt;i&gt;exceeded 86 degrees.&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:23.952 --> 00:44:25.746
&lt;i&gt;Feng Lianjin and his companions&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:25.746 --> 00:44:27.289
&lt;i&gt;hid in the shade of the bus&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:27.748 --> 00:44:30.250
&lt;i&gt;and discussed whether&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;they should get haircuts&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:30.250 --> 00:44:31.585
&lt;i&gt;while waiting for the bus.&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:31.585 --> 00:44:34.338
[Feng] I don’t know if there’s still time or not.

00:44:34.338 --> 00:44:36.298
[Feng’s friend] There should be time.

00:44:36.298 --> 00:44:37.925
Why don’t you let that barber friend

00:44:37.925 --> 00:44:40.177
give you a haircut?

00:44:41.595 --> 00:44:44.014
Give him a try.

00:44:45.557 --> 00:44:47.476
I don't know what we can do
when we arrive.

00:44:48.727 --> 00:44:50.813
If he does a good job,

00:44:50.813 --> 00:44:52.106
he can work at a barber shop.

00:44:53.023 --> 00:44:56.777
[Feng] &lt;i&gt;Yesterday I met an African.&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:58.112 --> 00:45:00.197
&lt;i&gt;From Guinea.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:01.657 --> 00:45:03.659
&lt;i&gt;He suddenly asked where we were from.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:04.243 --> 00:45:05.661
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;In Chinese?&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:06.370 --> 00:45:09.081
[Feng] &lt;i&gt;I asked, why can you speak Chinese?&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:09.081 --> 00:45:10.416
&lt;i&gt;Did you study in China?&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:10.416 --> 00:45:11.542
&lt;i&gt;He said yes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:12.668 --> 00:45:14.962
&lt;i&gt;I said, your Chinese is so good,&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:14.962 --> 00:45:16.088
&lt;i&gt;why didn’t you stay in China?&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:17.089 --> 00:45:20.801
&lt;i&gt;And he said, why didn't you stay in China?&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:26.390 --> 00:45:28.809
Do they call our names or what?

00:45:29.184 --> 00:45:29.643
I don’t know,

00:45:29.643 --> 00:45:31.520
he just asked us to come over
with the tickets.

00:45:37.192 --> 00:45:38.819
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Feng Lianjin's bus was stopped&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;by the immigration bureau&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:38.819 --> 00:45:40.487
&lt;i&gt;halfway along the journey,&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:40.487 --> 00:45:43.115
&lt;i&gt;and they were sent back&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to southern Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:43.115 --> 00:45:45.409
&lt;i&gt;Fortunately, he was not detained.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:45.409 --> 00:45:47.745
&lt;i&gt;Some are sent to immigration prisons&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:47.745 --> 00:45:49.413
&lt;i&gt;for a couple of weeks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:49.413 --> 00:45:51.540
&lt;i&gt;Sometimes they even have to pay a fee&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:51.540 --> 00:45:53.041
&lt;i&gt;before being released.&lt;/i&gt;

00:45:58.046 --> 00:46:01.049
&lt;i&gt;Some Chinese migrants make their faces darker&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:01.049 --> 00:46:02.634
&lt;i&gt;or wear football jerseys&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:02.634 --> 00:46:05.053
&lt;i&gt;to pretend to be Latinos to avoid interrogation.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:07.765 --> 00:46:09.016
[Yu] &lt;i&gt;I used it all the time in Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:09.016 --> 00:46:10.809
&lt;i&gt;Bought this in Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:12.019 --> 00:46:13.562
&lt;i&gt;What's this called? Foundation cream?&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:15.022 --> 00:46:17.733
&lt;i&gt;I used translation software to ask him&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:17.733 --> 00:46:19.902
&lt;i&gt;how do I make myself look tanner.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:19.902 --> 00:46:22.279
&lt;i&gt;Then the cosmetics seller&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;looked at me astonished.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:24.740 --> 00:46:26.950
&lt;i&gt;Then the first store wouldn’t sell it to me,&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:28.702
&lt;i&gt;but eventually the second store&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:28.702 --> 00:46:30.996
&lt;i&gt;sold it to me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:46:33.081 --> 00:46:36.084
I wouldn’t say 
 this is a discrimination,

00:46:36.084 --> 00:46:37.127
more a way

00:46:37.127 --> 00:46:41.340
these people are more bond to be abuse of Asians

00:46:41.340 --> 00:46:43.592
not only the Chinese, all Asians,

00:46:43.592 --> 00:46:45.344
from India, you name it.

00:46:45.344 --> 00:46:46.637
They (Mexican authorities or robbers)
would believe the same thing,

00:46:46.637 --> 00:46:47.596
They will say, well

00:46:47.596 --> 00:46:49.431
they (migrants) come all the way from India,

00:46:49.431 --> 00:46:51.558
so they must have more resources.

00:46:51.558 --> 00:46:54.102
Because they might think

00:46:54.102 --> 00:46:56.063
（migrants) they are not going to stay here anyway.

00:46:56.063 --> 00:46:57.731
They are going to travel to the US.

00:46:57.731 --> 00:46:59.817
so they would still have more money.

00:46:59.817 --> 00:47:01.777
or US dollars or whatever.

00:47:04.196 --> 00:47:06.323
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Lee and Ivan were asked for bribes&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:06.323 --> 00:47:10.118
&lt;i&gt;twice by the Mexican authorities.&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:10.118 --> 00:47:12.538
&lt;i&gt;They already learned to slip money&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:12.538 --> 00:47:13.705
&lt;i&gt;in their passports in advance&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:13.705 --> 00:47:14.873
&lt;i&gt;and hand them to the police.&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:15.374 --> 00:47:19.628
&lt;i&gt;[Chinatown Mexico City]&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:19.628 --> 00:47:21.463
&lt;i&gt;When we met them again,&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:21.463 --> 00:47:22.464
&lt;i&gt;Lee and Ivan had just been in line&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:22.464 --> 00:47:24.258
&lt;i&gt;for a few hours to receive&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:24.258 --> 00:47:26.260
&lt;i&gt;humanitarian passage documents.&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:26.260 --> 00:47:29.304
&lt;i&gt;Finally, they could travel legally in Mexico.&lt;/i&gt;

00:47:30.013 --> 00:47:31.807
[Alicia] When you got the papers,

00:47:31.807 --> 00:47:34.059
did you feel relieved?

00:47:38.772 --> 00:47:40.566
We must be about the same age.

00:47:42.192 --> 00:47:42.943
[Lee] He's the youngest.

00:47:44.069 --> 00:47:44.862
He's the eldest.

00:47:45.195 --> 00:47:45.821
[Alicia] How old are you?

00:47:46.071 --> 00:47:46.947
[Lee] He’s old.

00:47:47.990 --> 00:47:49.408
[Alicia] How can you call him old?

00:47:49.533 --> 00:47:51.994
[Cameraman] 35 is old? I'm also 35.

00:47:53.036 --> 00:47:54.830
Don’t live it up too much.

00:47:54.830 --> 00:47:56.665
Wait until you are more like
50 years old.

00:47:59.835 --> 00:48:01.378
If you don’t work hard
when you are young,

00:48:01.378 --> 00:48:02.838
you will have regrets
when you are old.

00:48:02.838 --> 00:48:04.673
I didn't work hard when I was young.

00:48:04.673 --> 00:48:05.966
I regretted it.

00:48:05.966 --> 00:48:07.467
[Lee] Your life is good!

00:48:09.636 --> 00:48:10.762
You need to work hard.

00:48:11.471 --> 00:48:13.557
Nowadays in China,
there are no more opportunities.

00:48:13.557 --> 00:48:14.933
When we were in China,

00:48:14.933 --> 00:48:15.851
when we were your age,

00:48:15.851 --> 00:48:17.352
there were too many opportunities.

00:48:19.354 --> 00:48:21.023
You could get interviews
from five or six different employers a day.

00:48:21.023 --> 00:48:22.107
They would all want you.

00:48:22.107 --> 00:48:24.359
You would think that's because
you were talented.

00:48:24.359 --> 00:48:26.737
But now all that’s dried up.

00:48:30.616 --> 00:48:32.910
Let’s find a coffee shop
to sit down and chat a bit.

00:48:41.168 --> 00:48:44.296
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;The road ahead is the home stretch.&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:44.296 --> 00:48:46.465
&lt;i&gt;Most migrants choose&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;a few major border cities&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:46.465 --> 00:48:48.759
&lt;i&gt;to cross over into the United States:&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:48.759 --> 00:48:49.551
&lt;i&gt;Tijuana,&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:49.885 --> 00:48:50.802
&lt;i&gt;Mexicali,&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:51.261 --> 00:48:52.220
&lt;i&gt;Ciudad Juárez,&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:52.346 --> 00:48:53.347
&lt;i&gt;and Monterrey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:56.642 --> 00:48:58.560
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;If you successfully make it to the US,&lt;/i&gt;

00:48:58.769 --> 00:49:00.228
&lt;i&gt;what do you think life will be like&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:00.228 --> 00:49:01.563
&lt;i&gt;for the two of you?&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:02.940 --> 00:49:04.816
[Lee] &lt;i&gt;First off, we are mentally prepared&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:04.816 --> 00:49:06.401
&lt;i&gt;for some hardship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:07.319 --> 00:49:09.571
&lt;i&gt;Some guy joked that he'll become&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:09.571 --> 00:49:11.698
&lt;i&gt;the dish washing master.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:11.698 --> 00:49:13.659
&lt;i&gt;It’s inevitable you have to do some&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:13.659 --> 00:49:14.868
&lt;i&gt;entry-level work at first.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:14.868 --> 00:49:17.329
&lt;i&gt;After obtaining work authorization,&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:17.329 --> 00:49:20.332
&lt;i&gt;then you might find some legal jobs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:22.876 --> 00:49:27.839
&lt;i&gt;After we have a stable job and income,&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:27.839 --> 00:49:31.218
&lt;i&gt;we can live like a normal married couple.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:31.218 --> 00:49:33.220
&lt;i&gt;Life will be good as long as we are together.&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:53.156 --> 00:49:54.908
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;Personally I think the border wall&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:54.908 --> 00:49:56.994
&lt;i&gt;sends a message&lt;/i&gt;

00:49:56.994 --> 00:50:00.163
&lt;i&gt;that you aren’t allowed to cross.&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:00.163 --> 00:50:01.164
&lt;i&gt;Right?&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:01.164 --> 00:50:03.458
&lt;i&gt;But why are there gaps?&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:03.458 --> 00:50:05.252
&lt;i&gt;That means,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;if you really want to come,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:05.252 --> 00:50:06.628
&lt;i&gt;I can also let you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:06.628 --> 00:50:08.672
&lt;i&gt;Like raising the gun muzzle up&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;an inch higher.&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:08.672 --> 00:50:10.007
&lt;i&gt;My attitude is no,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:10.007 --> 00:50:12.634
&lt;i&gt;but if you are serious&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:12.634 --> 00:50:13.468
&lt;i&gt;about crossing,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:13.468 --> 00:50:14.636
&lt;i&gt;I’ll let you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:20.600 --> 00:50:22.686
[Yu] Behind me is the

00:50:22.686 --> 00:50:24.187
Monterrey bus station.

00:50:26.189 --> 00:50:28.191
This afternoon

00:50:28.191 --> 00:50:29.818
I’ll cross the border.

00:50:29.818 --> 00:50:32.070
and enter the United States.

00:50:32.863 --> 00:50:34.448
I would be arrested for holding up

00:50:34.448 --> 00:50:36.533
such a piece of paper in China.

00:50:36.533 --> 00:50:37.659
Now I’ll turn it over

00:50:37.659 --> 00:50:39.286
and let everyone have a look.

00:50:40.537 --> 00:50:44.833
[Xi Jinping, you forbade me to vote with my hands,
now I vote with my feet.]

00:50:47.335 --> 00:50:48.879
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;By the end of April,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:48.879 --> 00:50:50.964
&lt;i&gt;all the Chinese migrants we filmed&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:50.964 --> 00:50:52.924
&lt;i&gt;came to the US-Mexico border&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;one after another.&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:53.967 --> 00:50:55.135
&lt;i&gt;If they are lucky,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:55.135 --> 00:50:57.512
&lt;i&gt;they can cross the border in a single day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:50:57.512 --> 00:51:00.140
&lt;i&gt;but they may also have to&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;hide in the bushes&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:00.140 --> 00:51:02.934
&lt;i&gt;for more than a week&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to avoid Mexican border police.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:11.234 --> 00:51:12.652
[Cindy]&lt;i&gt; I don’t know how long they’d been driving.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:12.652 --> 00:51:16.156
&lt;i&gt;We were in the car from&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;early morning to late at night.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:16.156 --> 00:51:18.366
&lt;i&gt;Then we walked to a very dark place,&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:18.366 --> 00:51:20.327
&lt;i&gt;but ultimately,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;we were spotted by the Mexican police.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:20.327 --> 00:51:22.329
&lt;i&gt;We had to run.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:22.329 --> 00:51:25.624
&lt;i&gt;That section of road was uneven&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:25.624 --> 00:51:28.502
&lt;i&gt;and there were a lot of cactus thorns,&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:28.502 --> 00:51:30.378
&lt;i&gt;I stepped in five of them.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:30.378 --> 00:51:33.340
&lt;i&gt;They went right into the sole of my foot.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:33.340 --> 00:51:34.508
&lt;i&gt;It hurt so much,&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:34.508 --> 00:51:36.134
&lt;i&gt;but I didn’t dare scream.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:36.134 --> 00:51:38.220
&lt;i&gt;I don’t know how long we waited.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:39.387
&lt;i&gt;I just lay on the ground.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:39.387 --> 00:51:41.306
&lt;i&gt;I lay my head on a bag&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;and looked up at the sky.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:41.306 --> 00:51:43.975
&lt;i&gt;It was such a starry night.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:43.975 --> 00:51:46.812
&lt;i&gt;Everyone else was wondering&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;whether the police had left.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:46.812 --> 00:51:48.396
&lt;i&gt;whether they could keep going.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:48.396 --> 00:51:49.314
&lt;i&gt;But I wasn't thinking about that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:49.314 --> 00:51:51.316
&lt;i&gt;At that moment,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;I just lay there quietly&lt;/i&gt;

00:51:51.316 --> 00:51:53.860
&lt;i&gt;and enjoyed the tranquility&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;of that moment.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:01.535 --> 00:52:03.078
[Yu] &lt;i&gt;You wait for a car&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in the afternoon,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:03.078 --> 00:52:05.956
&lt;i&gt;and it takes you directly to another place.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:05.956 --> 00:52:07.624
&lt;i&gt;Then you change cars again,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:07.624 --> 00:52:08.834
&lt;i&gt;and again.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:08.834 --> 00:52:10.127
&lt;i&gt;Then you arrive at the border.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:11.002 --> 00:52:11.962
&lt;i&gt;When we arrived at the border,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:11.962 --> 00:52:13.380
&lt;i&gt;we just waited by the river,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:14.923
&lt;i&gt;where drones and helicopters&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:14.923 --> 00:52:16.800
&lt;i&gt;were flying all around.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:18.969
&lt;i&gt;I forgot whether it was half an hour&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;or an hour.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:19.553 --> 00:52:20.762
&lt;i&gt;They send them out in groups,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:20.762 --> 00:52:23.557
&lt;i&gt;in a small boat,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:23.557 --> 00:52:24.975
&lt;i&gt;which could only hold about&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:24.975 --> 00:52:26.434
&lt;i&gt;a dozen people at a time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:27.144 --> 00:52:28.812
&lt;i&gt;They were taking drugs&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:28.812 --> 00:52:30.856
&lt;i&gt;while smuggling us.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:31.439 --> 00:52:32.732
&lt;i&gt;A bunch of drug addicts.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:33.775 --> 00:52:35.235
&lt;i&gt;The boat had an engine&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:35.235 --> 00:52:36.570
&lt;i&gt;that needed constant pulling.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:36.570 --> 00:52:37.737
&lt;i&gt;In the end they couldn't even&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:37.737 --> 00:52:38.864
&lt;i&gt;crank up the engine anymore.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:45.662 --> 00:52:47.330
[Cindy] &lt;i&gt;You just keep marching forward,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:47.330 --> 00:52:48.748
&lt;i&gt;and now you’re&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;at the end of the journey,&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:48.748 --> 00:52:50.292
&lt;i&gt;and you see the US is right over there.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:50.959 --> 00:52:52.794
&lt;i&gt;You still have to be miserable&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:52.794 --> 00:52:53.837
&lt;i&gt;to get across the finish line.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:54.838 --> 00:52:57.674
&lt;i&gt;Have you seen a safety ring like a tire?&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:57.674 --> 00:52:59.634
&lt;i&gt;They inflated the tire.&lt;/i&gt;

00:52:59.634 --> 00:53:01.386
&lt;i&gt;We held on to it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:01.386 --> 00:53:03.722
&lt;i&gt;Swam like kids, paddling.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:03.722 --> 00:53:05.182
&lt;i&gt;If you could swim, you'd swim over.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:05.682 --> 00:53:09.186
&lt;i&gt;And climb up onto the shore yourself.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:10.020 --> 00:53:13.231
&lt;i&gt;Then you see the cornfield.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:13.231 --> 00:53:14.316
&lt;i&gt;Texas is on the other side&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:14.316 --> 00:53:15.483
&lt;i&gt;of the cornfield.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:30.498 --> 00:53:32.667
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;After arriving in the United States,&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:32.667 --> 00:53:33.752
&lt;i&gt;Chinese migrants are quickly taken&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:33.752 --> 00:53:34.961
&lt;i&gt;to an immigration detention center&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:34.961 --> 00:53:36.463
&lt;i&gt;by US Border Patrol&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:36.463 --> 00:53:37.297
&lt;i&gt;and temporarily lose contact&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:37.297 --> 00:53:39.049
&lt;i&gt;with the outside world.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:39.049 --> 00:53:40.634
&lt;i&gt;It wasn’t until a week later&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:40.634 --> 00:53:43.220
&lt;i&gt;that I finally received news from everyone.&lt;/i&gt;

00:53:48.850 --> 00:53:51.686
[Ding’s Douyin] We’re here! Here!

00:53:51.686 --> 00:53:53.355
We made it!

00:53:53.355 --> 00:53:56.399
We made it to the US!

00:53:57.901 --> 00:54:00.111
[Lee] &lt;i&gt;I was worried for a few days.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:00.695 --> 00:54:01.529
&lt;i&gt;When I got out,&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:01.529 --> 00:54:04.658
&lt;i&gt;both our parents were relieved.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:04.658 --> 00:54:05.700
&lt;i&gt;He was relieved too.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:08.286 --> 00:54:10.664
[man with foot injury] &lt;i&gt;When I saw&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;the American flag waving,&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:10.664 --> 00:54:13.917
&lt;i&gt;I felt very excited and energized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:15.293 --> 00:54:17.712
&lt;i&gt;All the suffering I have experienced&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:17.712 --> 00:54:19.506
&lt;i&gt;is worth&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:19.506 --> 00:54:21.091
&lt;i&gt;what I have today.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:26.972 --> 00:54:29.099
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;This is f**king America.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:29.099 --> 00:54:29.933
&lt;i&gt;I wanted to swear.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:29.933 --> 00:54:32.686
&lt;i&gt;This is f**king America.&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:32.686 --> 00:54:34.479
&lt;i&gt;How on earth did I make it to the US?&lt;/i&gt;

00:54:35.605 --> 00:54:40.652
[“American Dream” by The Talbott Brothers playing]

00:55:39.210 --> 00:55:40.503
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Arriving in the US&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:40.503 --> 00:55:43.214
&lt;i&gt;does not mean the end of their journey,&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:43.214 --> 00:55:44.716
&lt;i&gt;but the beginning of their&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:44.716 --> 00:55:46.134
&lt;i&gt;long immigration journey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:47.052 --> 00:55:48.470
&lt;i&gt;Eight months later,&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:48.470 --> 00:55:50.388
&lt;i&gt;I met with them again to find out&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:50.388 --> 00:55:53.350
&lt;i&gt;how they were doing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:55.810
&lt;i&gt;Was it as good as they had expected?&lt;/i&gt;

00:55:56.144 --> 00:55:58.229
[pastor] Thank you for giving us your sustenance,

00:55:58.229 --> 00:56:01.107
so that we can truly feel God’s love

00:56:01.107 --> 00:56:03.068
through this food today.

00:56:03.068 --> 00:56:05.111
Thank you Lord for being with us

00:56:05.111 --> 00:56:07.405
and blessing us, continuing to

00:56:07.405 --> 00:56:09.282
lead us at noon today.

00:56:09.282 --> 00:56:10.700
Thank you Lord for hearing our prayers,

00:56:10.700 --> 00:56:12.160
in the name of Jesus Christ,

00:56:12.369 --> 00:56:12.869
Amen.

00:56:12.994 --> 00:56:13.703
Amen.

00:56:23.338 --> 00:56:25.382
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Not long after Yu Chunfei arrived,&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:25.382 --> 00:56:27.258
&lt;i&gt;he joined a Chinese church&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:27.258 --> 00:56:29.010
&lt;i&gt;and was baptized as a Christian.&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:29.719 --> 00:56:31.179
&lt;i&gt;He feels that in addition to&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:31.179 --> 00:56:32.472
&lt;i&gt;having a local community&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:32.472 --> 00:56:34.099
&lt;i&gt;that can provide support,&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:34.099 --> 00:56:35.892
&lt;i&gt;it can also be one of the reasons&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:35.892 --> 00:56:37.394
&lt;i&gt;for applying for asylum in the US.&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:39.020 --> 00:56:40.939
[Yu]&lt;i&gt; I volunteer three days a week.&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:41.189 --> 00:56:42.690
&lt;i&gt;Usually I can come twice a week.&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:43.108 --> 00:56:46.027
&lt;i&gt;I help with cleaning&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;on Wednesdays and Fridays.&lt;/i&gt;

00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:50.407
He’s our family.

00:56:50.407 --> 00:56:52.242
We are all one family.

00:56:52.617 --> 00:56:53.952
Because we all have

00:56:53.952 --> 00:56:55.120
the same Father in Heaven.

00:56:55.662 --> 00:56:57.205
The sunshine in California

00:56:57.205 --> 00:56:58.623
is itself a blessing.

00:57:00.166 --> 00:57:02.210
I think about

00:57:02.502 --> 00:57:04.629
how I want to live in the United States.

00:57:04.629 --> 00:57:05.797
After I get my work authorization,

00:57:05.797 --> 00:57:06.881
I want to take the driving exam

00:57:06.881 --> 00:57:08.341
and drive a big truck.

00:57:08.883 --> 00:57:10.552
I like my life in the US.

00:57:10.552 --> 00:57:11.928
But not speaking English

00:57:11.928 --> 00:57:13.721
makes life difficult.

00:57:17.642 --> 00:57:19.644
[Feng] Forty on No. 2.

00:57:24.858 --> 00:57:26.401
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;While Feng Lianjin was waiting for&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:26.401 --> 00:57:28.278
&lt;i&gt;his work authorization to be issued,&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:28.278 --> 00:57:29.612
&lt;i&gt;he got his driver's license&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:29.612 --> 00:57:31.281
&lt;i&gt;and started delivering packages for a living.&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:32.699 --> 00:57:35.285
[Feng] &lt;i&gt;These express deliveries&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:35.285 --> 00:57:37.036
&lt;i&gt;for Temu and Shein,&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:37.036 --> 00:57:38.204
&lt;i&gt;they came here to develop&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:38.204 --> 00:57:39.873
&lt;i&gt;these businesses,&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:39.873 --> 00:57:41.040
&lt;i&gt;and they needed to recruit&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:41.040 --> 00:57:43.001
&lt;i&gt;a lot of delivery guys.&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:43.001 --> 00:57:44.043
&lt;i&gt;Express delivery is&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:44.043 --> 00:57:46.171
&lt;i&gt;a job with a relatively low barrier to entry.&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:46.171 --> 00:57:47.672
&lt;i&gt;All you need is a car&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:47.672 --> 00:57:49.007
&lt;i&gt;and a driver's license.&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:49.007 --> 00:57:51.634
&lt;i&gt;It feels like they are a little crazier&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:51.634 --> 00:57:56.848
&lt;i&gt;than when we first arrived.&lt;/i&gt;

00:57:56.848 --> 00:57:59.851
There are many drivers who are older

00:57:59.851 --> 00:58:01.811
and have gray hair.

00:58:01.811 --> 00:58:04.189
Suddenly, the competition is growing.

00:58:04.189 --> 00:58:07.108
And now the unit price is relatively low,

00:58:07.108 --> 00:58:08.985
We are being exploited.

00:58:08.985 --> 00:58:10.820
I used to get paid two dollars per delivery,

00:58:10.820 --> 00:58:12.739
but now it's only 1.80 dollar.

00:58:12.739 --> 00:58:14.324
So if you wanted to make
200 dollars per day,

00:58:14.324 --> 00:58:15.742
you would need to deliver

00:58:15.742 --> 00:58:18.536
about 100 packages.

00:58:18.536 --> 00:58:20.330
Before, I needed to deliver 100 packages,

00:58:20.330 --> 00:58:21.372
now it’s about 110.

00:58:22.790 --> 00:58:24.834
Too many Chinese here now.

00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:26.878
Everyone wants a job.

00:58:26.878 --> 00:58:28.254
Seeing so many Chinese,

00:58:28.254 --> 00:58:29.380
I feel like I want to go back to China.

00:58:33.301 --> 00:58:35.678
[Feng] &lt;i&gt;My family started persuading me&lt;/i&gt;

00:58:35.678 --> 00:58:38.473
&lt;i&gt;to go back as soon as I set out&lt;/i&gt;

00:58:38.473 --> 00:58:41.768
&lt;i&gt;and kept at it my entire journey.&lt;/i&gt;

00:58:41.768 --> 00:58:44.896
&lt;i&gt;But once I got here and settled down,&lt;/i&gt;

00:58:44.896 --> 00:58:46.189
&lt;i&gt;they let up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:58:49.734 --> 00:58:51.027
Once he enters the United States,

00:58:51.027 --> 00:58:52.445
he will be protected by

00:58:52.445 --> 00:58:53.988
the 14th Amendment to the Constitution.

00:58:53.988 --> 00:58:55.823
He and everyone else,

00:58:55.823 --> 00:58:57.534
just the same as Biden and Trump,

00:58:57.534 --> 00:59:00.036
have the right to equal protection

00:59:00.036 --> 00:59:01.746
and the right to due process.

00:59:02.497 --> 00:59:04.916
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Immigration lawyer&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Huang Xiaosheng explained that&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:04.916 --> 00:59:06.459
&lt;i&gt;the lengthy legal process&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:06.459 --> 00:59:08.878
&lt;i&gt;has a huge impact on the lives&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;of immigrants.&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:09.420 --> 00:59:10.588
During the entire process,

00:59:10.588 --> 00:59:12.882
his time in the United States

00:59:12.882 --> 00:59:17.512
will be roughly three years at minimum,

00:59:17.512 --> 00:59:19.847
eight years if it’s slow,

00:59:19.847 --> 00:59:21.683
but possibly up to 10 years.

00:59:21.683 --> 00:59:23.601
Eight to ten years is at least

00:59:23.601 --> 00:59:25.603
one-eighth of his life.

00:59:25.603 --> 00:59:27.063
He can raise his children here,

00:59:27.063 --> 00:59:28.690
run a company here,

00:59:28.690 --> 00:59:31.067
and drive a truck here to do business.

00:59:31.067 --> 00:59:33.736
His life will undergo major changes.

00:59:33.736 --> 00:59:35.321
His home country may

00:59:35.321 --> 00:59:37.282
become farther and farther away,

00:59:37.282 --> 00:59:38.700
so the United States has allowed him

00:59:38.700 --> 00:59:40.243
to put down roots.

00:59:47.667 --> 00:59:49.502
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; New York is another city&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:49.502 --> 00:59:51.379
&lt;i&gt;that Chinese migrants are drawn to.&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:51.379 --> 00:59:52.839
&lt;i&gt;There are many immigrants here&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:52.839 --> 00:59:54.674
&lt;i&gt;and there are many job opportunities.&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:54.674 --> 00:59:57.635
&lt;i&gt;The colorful fluorescent screens&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;in Times Square&lt;/i&gt;

00:59:57.635 --> 01:00:00.847
&lt;i&gt;feel like the image of the United States&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:00.847 --> 01:00:03.308
&lt;i&gt;that Chinese migrants had in their minds&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;before arrival.&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:07.061 --> 01:00:08.730
&lt;i&gt;After a few transfers on the subway,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:08.730 --> 01:00:11.774
&lt;i&gt;I arrived in New York's Chinatown, Flushing.&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:11.774 --> 01:00:13.651
&lt;i&gt;Unlike in Times Square,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:13.651 --> 01:00:15.486
&lt;i&gt;the people walking on the streets here,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:15.486 --> 01:00:17.238
&lt;i&gt;the shop signs,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:17.238 --> 01:00:20.116
&lt;i&gt;and the occasional conversations&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;from passers-by remind me&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:20.116 --> 01:00:22.452
&lt;i&gt;more of a small county in China&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:22.452 --> 01:00:24.245
&lt;i&gt;with stagnant economic development&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:24.245 --> 01:00:25.538
&lt;i&gt;than the United States.&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:29.626 --> 01:00:30.793
Hi!

01:00:33.463 --> 01:00:35.882
[Alicia] Long time no see.

01:00:35.882 --> 01:00:37.759
So cold today. Are you alright?

01:00:37.759 --> 01:00:39.510
What do you do for work now?

01:00:39.510 --> 01:00:41.304
Looks difficult.

01:00:42.180 --> 01:00:43.264
[man with foot injury] It’s ok.

01:00:43.264 --> 01:00:45.850
I work at a restaurant.

01:00:46.434 --> 01:00:47.727
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; Because of his foot injury,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:47.727 --> 01:00:49.562
&lt;i&gt;he quickly received Medicaid&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:49.562 --> 01:00:50.855
&lt;i&gt;from New York State,&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:51.481 --> 01:00:54.150
&lt;i&gt;and applied for political asylum.&lt;/i&gt;

01:00:55.193 --> 01:00:57.904
[man with foot injury] The master calendar
hearing was held.

01:00:57.987 --> 01:01:00.073
[Alicia] Are you waiting for
the individual hearing?

01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:03.910
Do you know the time for that?

01:01:04.702 --> 01:01:05.202
[man with foot injury] No.

01:01:05.244 --> 01:01:06.746
[Alicia] Not yet? Still waiting.

01:01:07.705 --> 01:01:10.083
That’s not so bad, right?

01:01:18.925 --> 01:01:20.176
[man with foot injury] All in all,

01:01:20.927 --> 01:01:23.262
the humanitarian assistance here

01:01:23.888 --> 01:01:26.140
is still very good,

01:01:26.599 --> 01:01:28.351
even for people like us

01:01:28.351 --> 01:01:30.728
who entered the United States illegally.

01:01:32.397 --> 01:01:35.358
[Alicia] Did you get treatment for your foot?

01:01:35.358 --> 01:01:35.942
Yeah. They treated it.

01:01:36.818 --> 01:01:37.819
[Alicia] That’s good.

01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:41.239
[man with foot injury] I have always longed for

01:01:44.701 --> 01:01:48.621
a democratic and free country.

01:01:48.913 --> 01:01:51.249
That doesn’t discriminate against

01:01:51.249 --> 01:01:52.542
disadvantaged groups.

01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:53.960
To be honest,

01:01:53.960 --> 01:01:57.088
if you don’t have a very

01:01:57.088 --> 01:01:59.674
privileged family,

01:01:59.674 --> 01:02:02.135
or if you don’t have exceptional talent

01:02:02.135 --> 01:02:04.262
in a certain field,

01:02:05.722 --> 01:02:08.891
such as academically,

01:02:08.891 --> 01:02:10.685
it would be almost impossible

01:02:10.685 --> 01:02:12.729
to come to the United States.

01:02:13.896 --> 01:02:16.023
Except in this way.

01:02:16.983 --> 01:02:19.736
[Alicia] What is your dream here?

01:02:19.736 --> 01:02:24.699
[man with foot injury] My dream is
to have a business here,

01:02:24.699 --> 01:02:25.658
my very own.

01:02:34.083 --> 01:02:36.627
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Cindy, the girl we met on the road,&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:36.627 --> 01:02:38.963
&lt;i&gt;rents a house in Flushing&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:38.963 --> 01:02:40.965
&lt;i&gt;with other Chinese immigrants.&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:40.965 --> 01:02:43.634
&lt;i&gt;A private room costs&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;700 dollars per month.&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:43.634 --> 01:02:47.513
&lt;i&gt;She usually commutes by kick scooter and bus.&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:47.513 --> 01:02:48.931
&lt;i&gt;For several months,&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:48.931 --> 01:02:50.475
&lt;i&gt;she has been looking for a job&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:50.475 --> 01:02:52.643
&lt;i&gt;on Chinese information platforms.&lt;/i&gt;

01:02:52.643 --> 01:02:55.313
I’ve viewed every post on this website.

01:02:57.648 --> 01:03:00.193
I've asked all of these.

01:03:00.193 --> 01:03:01.235
All rejected.

01:03:01.235 --> 01:03:02.570
They want someone with experience,

01:03:02.570 --> 01:03:03.529
or who can file taxes.

01:03:04.238 --> 01:03:06.407
I can’t apply.

01:03:07.658 --> 01:03:08.618
You see?

01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:09.577
So many.

01:03:10.870 --> 01:03:12.288
I’ve been asking for jobs

01:03:12.288 --> 01:03:13.748
for a long time, but got no responses.

01:03:16.501 --> 01:03:18.336
These are the early messages.

01:03:19.545 --> 01:03:21.923
I applied for so many.

01:03:23.591 --> 01:03:24.342
All rejected.

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:27.345
Everyday...

01:03:30.056 --> 01:03:31.224
I search again and again.

01:03:32.850 --> 01:03:35.686
Whenever I’m free I’m searching for jobs.

01:03:36.771 --> 01:03:39.565
I only tell my family good news.

01:03:41.067 --> 01:03:42.151
Painkillers.

01:03:42.151 --> 01:03:44.445
It costs me 25 dollars, so expensive.

01:03:46.072 --> 01:03:48.282
[Alicia]&lt;i&gt; Cindy stayed in the thick forest&lt;/i&gt;

01:03:48.282 --> 01:03:50.117
&lt;i&gt;on the US-Mexico border&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for nine days,&lt;/i&gt;

01:03:50.117 --> 01:03:52.203
&lt;i&gt;and the foot injury she got then&lt;/i&gt;

01:03:52.203 --> 01:03:54.247
&lt;i&gt;continues to affect her life.&lt;/i&gt;

01:03:55.206 --> 01:03:56.541
What do you think made you

01:03:56.541 --> 01:03:58.501
persist in getting here

01:03:58.501 --> 01:04:02.588
and then continue to try to stay?

01:04:02.588 --> 01:04:06.133
What motivates you?

01:04:06.133 --> 01:04:07.343
A belief.

01:04:09.720 --> 01:04:13.140
Just like what I told you over there,

01:04:14.016 --> 01:04:15.560
I said that I yearn for freedom.

01:04:16.185 --> 01:04:18.229
I think I can be free here.

01:04:19.146 --> 01:04:21.065
That’s why I persisted

01:04:21.065 --> 01:04:21.941
in coming.

01:04:23.109 --> 01:04:25.820
It’s actually very freeing.

01:04:25.820 --> 01:04:26.779
Why?

01:04:26.779 --> 01:04:28.573
Everyone is minding their own business.

01:04:28.573 --> 01:04:30.157
No one cares about you at all.

01:04:30.157 --> 01:04:31.826
How can you not be free?

01:05:02.732 --> 01:05:06.402
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;When I met up with Lee and Ivan again,&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:06.402 --> 01:05:08.738
&lt;i&gt;they agreed to appear on camera.&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:09.864 --> 01:05:12.867
[Lee] We are legally married here.

01:05:12.867 --> 01:05:16.537
We want to let people like us know

01:05:16.537 --> 01:05:20.249
of our experiences.

01:05:20.249 --> 01:05:22.627
They can also consider getting married

01:05:22.627 --> 01:05:23.878
somewhere else.

01:05:23.878 --> 01:05:26.714
[Ivan] I hope LGBTQ+ people in China know

01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:29.675
that they can if they want to.

01:05:31.177 --> 01:05:33.387
There are more options,

01:05:33.387 --> 01:05:34.722
if they want to.

01:05:34.722 --> 01:05:36.724
We want to offer our experience
for their consideration.

01:05:38.392 --> 01:05:41.562
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;They found jobs in a dessert shop in New York,&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:41.562 --> 01:05:42.939
&lt;i&gt;rented a place together,&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:42.939 --> 01:05:45.149
&lt;i&gt;and got married successfully.&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:45.149 --> 01:05:47.777
&lt;i&gt;Everything seems to be on track,&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:47.777 --> 01:05:52.281
&lt;i&gt;but sometimes they still&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;miss their life in China,&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:52.281 --> 01:05:55.201
&lt;i&gt;especially their family and their six dogs.&lt;/i&gt;

01:05:58.162 --> 01:06:00.081
It’s very difficult.

01:06:00.081 --> 01:06:01.624
You miss your dogs.

01:06:01.624 --> 01:06:05.044
Aww, gentleman.

01:06:08.923 --> 01:06:10.466
Is it a boy or a girl?

01:06:10.466 --> 01:06:11.342
Boy.

01:06:11.342 --> 01:06:12.885
He looks exactly like her.

01:06:12.885 --> 01:06:14.303
Are they the same size？

01:06:15.179 --> 01:06:17.264
Say hello.

01:06:20.559 --> 01:06:21.978
She loves her cheeks.

01:06:21.978 --> 01:06:24.021
She loves a butt scratch too.

01:06:24.522 --> 01:06:26.857
He just sheds a lot.

01:06:32.947 --> 01:06:34.115
[Lee] &lt;i&gt;I think the situation here in the US&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:34.115 --> 01:06:35.533
&lt;i&gt;is actually not much different from&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:35.533 --> 01:06:36.826
&lt;i&gt;what I had imagined before.&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:37.493 --> 01:06:38.911
&lt;i&gt;The US developed relatively early,&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:38.911 --> 01:06:40.496
&lt;i&gt;its infrastructure may look relatively old,&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:42.790
&lt;i&gt;but what can I say?&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:42.790 --> 01:06:45.042
&lt;i&gt;The subway operates 24 hours a day,&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:45.167 --> 01:06:46.043
&lt;i&gt;which I didn’t expect.&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:46.168 --> 01:06:47.962
&lt;i&gt;I thought it would just stop running at midnight,&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:47.962 --> 01:06:49.171
&lt;i&gt;just like in China.&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:49.255 --> 01:06:52.091
&lt;i&gt;Other aspects are similar to what I expected,&lt;/i&gt;

01:06:52.091 --> 01:06:55.011
&lt;i&gt;including our jobs.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:12.445 --> 01:07:15.656
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Lawyer Huang, who is a first-generation&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;immigrant himself,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:15.656 --> 01:07:19.285
&lt;i&gt;once read me the famous inscription&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;on the Statue of Liberty.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:21.829 --> 01:07:24.832
[Huang] &lt;i&gt;Give me your tired,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:24.832 --> 01:07:26.917
&lt;i&gt;your poor,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:26.917 --> 01:07:30.671
&lt;i&gt;your huddled masses yearning to breathe free.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:30.671 --> 01:07:33.215
&lt;i&gt;your huddled masses yearning to breathe free.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:33.215 --> 01:07:35.801
&lt;i&gt;It means, if you are oppressed, come to America.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:38.429 --> 01:07:40.931
&lt;i&gt;Mr. Li, who once said that the Statue of Liberty&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:40.931 --> 01:07:42.933
&lt;i&gt;was calling him to come to the US,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:44.477
&lt;i&gt;refused to meet with me.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:45.561 --> 01:07:47.730
[Mr. Li] &lt;i&gt;The American dream&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:47.730 --> 01:07:49.899
&lt;i&gt;that I had completely shattered,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:49.899 --> 01:07:52.985
&lt;i&gt;and it’s not as beautiful as I imagined.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:52.985 --> 01:07:55.362
&lt;i&gt;I'm completely working class here,&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:55.362 --> 01:07:57.615
&lt;i&gt;at the bottom rung of society.&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:57.615 --> 01:07:59.492
&lt;i&gt;It's not as good as the inscription&lt;/i&gt;

01:07:59.492 --> 01:08:00.743
&lt;i&gt;on the Statue of Liberty.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:08.501 --> 01:08:10.586
[Cindy] &lt;i&gt;Life can't be measured by&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:10.586 --> 01:08:12.338
&lt;i&gt;whether it’s “worth it” or not.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:12.338 --> 01:08:14.590
&lt;i&gt;During this period,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:14.590 --> 01:08:15.216
&lt;i&gt;there were gains&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:15.216 --> 01:08:16.675
&lt;i&gt;and losses,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:16.675 --> 01:08:18.302
&lt;i&gt;and more importantly, sadness.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:19.762 --> 01:08:22.014
[Feng]&lt;i&gt; I think it’s probably worth it.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:22.014 --> 01:08:23.557
&lt;i&gt;If I had to choose again,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:23.557 --> 01:08:25.518
&lt;i&gt;I would still come here.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:25.518 --> 01:08:26.977
&lt;i&gt;After all,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:26.977 --> 01:08:30.523
&lt;i&gt;the three-year Zero-Covid period&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:30.523 --> 01:08:31.690
&lt;i&gt;was pretty harsh.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:33.317 --> 01:08:36.695
[Ding] &lt;i&gt;Hope is like planting a seed.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:36.695 --> 01:08:39.156
&lt;i&gt;It will grow without limit.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:43.035 --> 01:08:44.829
[Yu] &lt;i&gt;I think walking the line&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:44.829 --> 01:08:46.914
&lt;i&gt;was the best decision I've&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;ever made in my life.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:47.873 --> 01:08:50.292
[Lee] &lt;i&gt;You have to respect every choice&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;you make in your life.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:50.459 --> 01:08:51.710
&lt;i&gt;No matter where you go,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:52.044 --> 01:08:53.379
&lt;i&gt;you have to consider&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:53.379 --> 01:08:54.964
&lt;i&gt;whether you will regret&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:54.964 --> 01:08:56.632
&lt;i&gt;your decision in the future.&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:56.632 --> 01:08:59.009
&lt;i&gt;Don't regret the decision you made,&lt;/i&gt;

01:08:59.009 --> 01:09:00.219
&lt;i&gt;you can only look forward.&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:17.486 --> 01:09:19.572
[Alicia] &lt;i&gt;Even though I went through this journey&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:19.572 --> 01:09:22.283
&lt;i&gt;with these migrants,&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:22.283 --> 01:09:24.160
&lt;i&gt;I still can't imagine&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:24.160 --> 01:09:25.536
&lt;i&gt;how much more they will pay&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:25.536 --> 01:09:28.414
&lt;i&gt;for freedom.&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:28.414 --> 01:09:29.915
&lt;i&gt;Can this land&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:29.915 --> 01:09:32.960
&lt;i&gt;allow them to continue to live their lives here?&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:36.130 --> 01:09:39.175
-[Biden] &lt;i&gt;Today, I'm announcing actions to bar migrants&lt;/i&gt;
-[Trump] &lt;i&gt;Our border is an open and gushing wound.&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:39.175 --> 01:09:42.178
-[Biden] &lt;i&gt;who cross our southern border unlawfully&lt;/i&gt;
-[Trump] &lt;i&gt;It's pouring drugs, gangs, terrorists&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:42.178 --> 01:09:44.847
-[Biden] &lt;i&gt;from receiving asylum.&lt;/i&gt;
-[Trump] &lt;i&gt;and millions and millions of illegal aliens&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:44.847 --> 01:09:46.515
-[Biden] &lt;i&gt;from receiving asylum.&lt;/i&gt;
-[Trump] &lt;i&gt;into our country.&lt;/i&gt;

01:09:48.142 --> 01:10:00.279
Chinese Embassy Spokesperson's Remarks：
“The Chinese government firmly opposes all forms of illegal immigration... It should be noted that the issue of illegal immigration is an international one...China firmly opposes the US media and politicians using the issue as a pretext to smear and scapegoat China.”

01:10:01.697 --> 01:10:08.829
Many changes in every aspect of this route have occurred
 since we filmed the documentary, making the journey more difficult 
and more dangerous than ever.

